Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.85,0:00:20.23,Default,,0,0,0,,[Cheerful instrumental music]
Dialogue: 0,0:02:23.69,0:02:25.57,Default,,0,0,0,,[Clock dinging]
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.76,0:02:56.22,Default,,0,0,0,,[Children screaming]
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.30,0:02:58.26,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, what's it going to be?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.35,0:03:00.77,Default,,0,0,0,,A Triple Cream Cup for Christopher.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.97,0:03:03.43,Default,,0,0,0,,A Squelchy Snorter for Otis.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.52,0:03:06.69,Default,,0,0,0,,A Sizzler for June Marie. And listen.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.81,0:03:09.44,Default,,0,0,0,,BILL: Wonka's got a new one today.\NCHILDREN: What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.52,0:03:12.23,Default,,0,0,0,,This is called a Scrumdiddleumptious Bar.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.32,0:03:15.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Scrumdiddleumptious Bar?\NHow does he do it?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.15,0:03:17.99,Default,,0,0,0,,- My boy, do you ask a fish how it swims?\N- No.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.07,0:03:19.66,Default,,0,0,0,,BILL: Or a bird how it flies?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.74,0:03:22.91,Default,,0,0,0,,No sirree, you don't.\NThey do it because they were born to do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.00,0:03:26.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Just like Willy Wonka\Nwas born to be a candy man...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.29,0:03:29.17,Default,,0,0,0,,and you look like\Nyou were born to be a Wonkerer.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.25,0:03:32.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Singing] Who can take the sunrise{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.67,0:03:35.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Sprinkle it with dew{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.22,0:03:39.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Cover it in chocolate and a miracle or two?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.97,0:03:41.81,Default,,0,0,0,,The Candy Man.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.06,0:03:45.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Singing] The Candy Man can{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.56,0:03:49.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The Candy Man can\N'Cause he mixes it with love{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.52,0:03:51.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And makes the world taste good{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.69,0:03:56.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Who can take a rainbow{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.07,0:03:59.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Wrap it in a sigh{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.53,0:04:04.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Soak it in the sun\NAnd make the strawberry-lemon pie?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.37,0:04:07.04,Default,,0,0,0,,CHILDREN: The Candy Man?\NBILL: The Candy Man.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.42,0:04:10.26,Default,,0,0,0,,The Candy Man can.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.08,0:04:14.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Singing] The Candy Man can\N'Cause he mixes it with love{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.30,0:04:16.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And makes the world taste good{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.22,0:04:19.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Willy Wonka makes{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.89,0:04:21.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Everything he bakes{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.60,0:04:24.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Satisfying and delicious{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.02,0:04:27.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Talk about your childhood wishes{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.27,0:04:31.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You can even eat the dishes{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.19,0:04:37.32,Default,,0,0,0,,[Lively instrumental music]
Dialogue: 0,0:04:42.16,0:04:44.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Singing] Who can take tomorrow{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.54,0:04:46.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Dip it in a dream{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.41,0:04:50.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Separate the sorrow\Nand collect up all the cream?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.92,0:04:53.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}BILL: The Candy Man\NCHILDREN: Willy Wonka can{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.13,0:04:56.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The Candy Man can{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.09,0:05:02.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The Candy Man can\N'Cause he mixes it with love{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.30,0:05:06.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And makes the world taste good{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:07.81,0:05:09.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And the world tastes good{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.98,0:05:16.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}'Cause the Candy Man thinks it should{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.67,0:05:37.09,Default,,0,0,0,,CHARLIE: Hi, Mr. Jopeck.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.17,0:05:39.84,Default,,0,0,0,,MR. JOPECK: Come along, Charlie.\NYou're late.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.80,0:05:44.47,Default,,0,0,0,,CHARLIE: It's payday, Mr. Jopeck.\NMR. JOPECK: You're right.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.51,0:05:47.85,Default,,0,0,0,,MR. JOPECK: There you are.\NCHARLIE: Thanks.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.64,0:05:49.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Say hello to your Grandpa Joe.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.81,0:05:50.94,Default,,0,0,0,,CHARLIE: Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.15,0:05:55.57,Default,,0,0,0,,[Fast-paced instrumental music]
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.41,0:06:08.62,Default,,0,0,0,,[Eerie instrumental music]
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.89,0:06:36.02,Default,,0,0,0,,THE TINKER: " Up the airy mountain
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.23,0:06:38.48,Default,,0,0,0,," Down the rushing glen
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.69,0:06:40.86,Default,,0,0,0,," We dare not go a-hunting
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.03,0:06:43.95,Default,,0,0,0,," For fear of little men"
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.36,0:06:48.70,Default,,0,0,0,,You see, nobody ever goes in...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.16,0:06:54.20,Default,,0,0,0,,and nobody ever comes out.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.63,0:07:06.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Charlie's late.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.55,0:07:09.22,Default,,0,0,0,,He works too hard for a little boy.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.43,0:07:11.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}GRANDPA: He should have\Nsome time to play.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.52,0:07:13.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Not enough hours in the day.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.27,0:07:16.40,Default,,0,0,0,,MRS. BUCKET: With the four of you\Nbedridden for the past 20 years...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.48,0:07:18.98,Default,,0,0,0,,it takes a lot of work\Nto keep this family going.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:19.06,0:07:21.35,Default,,0,0,0,,If only his father were alive.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.94,0:07:25.69,Default,,0,0,0,,As soon as I get my strength back,\NI'll get out of this bed and help him.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.78,0:07:29.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}In all the years you've been saying\Nyou'll get out of that bed...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.32,0:07:32.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I've yet to see you set foot on the floor.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.25,0:07:35.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe if the floor wasn't so cold...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.25,0:07:38.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Hi, everybody.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.46,0:07:42.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Wake up, Charlie's home.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.42,0:07:44.96,Default,,0,0,0,,CHARLIE: Grandpa George.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.43,0:07:48.10,Default,,0,0,0,,CHARLIE: Grandma Georgina.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.43,0:07:50.18,Default,,0,0,0,,CHARLIE: Grandma Josephine.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.31,0:07:53.15,Default,,0,0,0,,CHARLIE: Grandpa Joe.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.60,0:07:57.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Is this your supper, Grandpa?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.94,0:07:59.69,Default,,0,0,0,,It's yours, too, Charlie.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.77,0:08:02.73,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm fed up with cabbage water.\NIt's not enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.82,0:08:05.41,Default,,0,0,0,,JOSEPHINE: It's all we have.\NGRANDPA: What are you saying?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.65,0:08:09.53,Default,,0,0,0,,CHARLIE: How about this?\NMRS. BUCKET: Where did you get that?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.62,0:08:13.21,Default,,0,0,0,,What difference does it make\Nwhere he got it? Point is, he got it.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:13.29,0:08:17.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}- It's my first payday.\N- Good for you. We'll have a real banquet.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.66,0:08:21.66,Default,,0,0,0,,CHARLIE: Mom, here's what's left.\NYou keep it.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.84,0:08:24.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Except for this.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.67,0:08:27.76,Default,,0,0,0,,From now on,\NI'm going to pay for your tobacco.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.68,0:08:31.98,Default,,0,0,0,,No one's going to pay for it.\NI'm giving it up.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.30,0:08:34.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, Dad, it's only one pipe a day.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.81,0:08:38.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}When a loaf of bread looks like a banquet,\NI've no right buying tobacco.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.52,0:08:41.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Go on, Grandpa. Please take it.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.20,0:08:53.00,Default,,0,0,0,,CHARLIE: After I finished my paper route,\NI was in front of Wonka's.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.49,0:08:57.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}There was this strange man there.\NI think he was a tinker.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.04,0:09:01.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He was standing right behind me\Nlooking up at the factory.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.67,0:09:03.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Just before he left, he said.:{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.00,0:09:07.30,Default,,0,0,0,," Nobody ever goes in,\Nand nobody ever comes out. "
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.51,0:09:09.47,Default,,0,0,0,,And right he was, Charlie.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.55,0:09:12.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Not since the tragic day\Nthat Willy Wonka locked it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.55,0:09:13.80,Default,,0,0,0,,CHARLIE: Why did he lock it?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.89,0:09:17.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Because all the other chocolate makers\Nwere sending in spies...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.39,0:09:20.85,Default,,0,0,0,,dressed as workers\Nto steal Mr. Wonka's secret recipes.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.06,0:09:25.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Especially Slugworth.\NThat Slugworth was the worst.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.57,0:09:29.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Finally, Mr. Wonka shouted,\N" I shall be ruined! Close the factory. "
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.95,0:09:32.45,Default,,0,0,0,,And that's just what he did.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.53,0:09:36.08,Default,,0,0,0,,He locked the gates\Nand vanished completely.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.37,0:09:39.33,Default,,0,0,0,,And then suddenly,\Nabout three years later...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.41,0:09:42.00,Default,,0,0,0,,the most amazing thing happened.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:42.21,0:09:44.96,Default,,0,0,0,,The factory started working again,\Nfull blast.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.04,0:09:48.50,Default,,0,0,0,,And more delicious candies\Nwere coming out than ever before.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.59,0:09:51.72,Default,,0,0,0,,But the gates stayed locked,\Nso that no one...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.93,0:09:54.81,Default,,0,0,0,,not even Mr. Slugworth, could steal them.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.89,0:09:59.02,Default,,0,0,0,,But, Grandpa, someone must be helping\NMr. Wonka work the factory.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.10,0:10:00.89,Default,,0,0,0,,GRANDPA: Thousands\Nmust be helping him.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.98,0:10:03.48,Default,,0,0,0,,But who? Who are they?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.44,0:10:07.69,Default,,0,0,0,,That is the biggest mystery of them all.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:09.65,0:10:11.74,Default,,0,0,0,,TURKENTINE: Charlie Bucket?\NCHARLIE: Yes, sir?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:11.82,0:10:15.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}TURKENTINE: I shall need an assistant.\NCome and give me a hand.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.16,0:10:19.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We have here nitric acid, glycerin...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.41,0:10:21.50,Default,,0,0,0,,and a special mixture of my own.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.58,0:10:24.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Together, it's horrible, dangerous stuff.\NBlows you up.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.67,0:10:28.09,Default,,0,0,0,,But mixed together right, as only\NI know how, what do you think it makes?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.17,0:10:30.34,Default,,0,0,0,,CHARLIE: I don't know.\NTURKENTINE: Of course not...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.42,0:10:32.01,Default,,0,0,0,,because only I know.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.09,0:10:35.76,Default,,0,0,0,,If you knew, you'd be teaching me\Ninstead of me teaching you.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:35.84,0:10:40.60,Default,,0,0,0,,And for a student to teach his teacher\Nis presumptuous and rude. Is that clear?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.68,0:10:42.02,Default,,0,0,0,,CHARLIE: Yes, sir.\NTURKENTINE: Good.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.10,0:10:46.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Mixed together in the right way,\Nthese three highly dangerous ingredients...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.90,0:10:49.28,Default,,0,0,0,,make the finest wart remover\Nin the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.36,0:10:52.11,Default,,0,0,0,,TURKENTINE: The trick is to pour them in\Nin equal amounts.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:52.19,0:10:55.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Charlie, you take the nitric acid\Nand the glycerin...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.57,0:10:58.74,Default,,0,0,0,,and I'll take my own special mixture.\NAre you ready?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:58.83,0:11:00.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Good lad. Pour.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.50,0:11:02.88,Default,,0,0,0,,[Students laughing and clapping]
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.96,0:11:04.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Did we do it wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.79,0:11:07.92,Default,,0,0,0,,TURKENTINE: No, certainly not.\NThis is for very big warts.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.13,0:11:10.55,Default,,0,0,0,,What on earth's going on out there?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:10.63,0:11:12.55,Default,,0,0,0,,STUDENT 1: I hope there's still some left.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:12.76,0:11:15.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Winkelmann, come here.\NWhat's happening?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.30,0:11:16.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Willy Wonka's opening his factory.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.84,0:11:19.01,Default,,0,0,0,,- He's gonna let people in.\N- Are you sure?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.10,0:11:21.56,Default,,0,0,0,,It's on the radio.\NAnd he's giving chocolates away.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.64,0:11:22.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Class dismissed.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.77,0:11:24.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}WINKELMANN: No, it's only for five people.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.60,0:11:26.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Class un-dismissed.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:26.35,0:11:29.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He's hidden five Golden Tickets.\NWhoever finds them wins the prize.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.98,0:11:32.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}- Where's he hidden them?\N- In five Wonka Bars.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:33.49,0:11:35.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}- You've gotta buy them to find them.\N- Class re-dismissed!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.12,0:11:41.29,Default,,0,0,0,,STUDENT 2: I'm going to buy\Nthe whole store.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.54,0:11:49.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}NEWSCASTER: Now, details\Non the sudden announcement...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.13,0:11:51.76,Default,,0,0,0,,that has captured the attention\Nof the entire world.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.84,0:11:54.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Hidden among the countless billions\Nof Wonka Bars...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.80,0:11:56.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}are five Gold Tickets.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.80,0:12:01.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And to the five people who find them\Nwill come the most fabulous prize:{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.35,0:12:03.77,Default,,0,0,0,,A lifetime supply of chocolate.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.85,0:12:05.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}As if this were not enough...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.73,0:12:09.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}each winner, before receiving his prize,\Nwill be personally escorted...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.81,0:12:11.44,Default,,0,0,0,,They're all crazy.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.52,0:12:14.86,Default,,0,0,0,,GRANDPA: The man's a genius.\NHe'll sell a million bars.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.69,0:12:18.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Grandpa, do you think I've got a chance\Nto find one?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.74,0:12:21.58,Default,,0,0,0,,One? I'm counting on you to find all five.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.66,0:12:23.04,Default,,0,0,0,,One's enough for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.12,0:12:26.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}NEWSCASTER: We have reports coming in\Nthat the response is phenomenal.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.46,0:12:29.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Wonka Bars are disappearing\Nfrom candy store shelves...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.58,0:12:31.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}at a rate to boggle the mind.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.67,0:12:33.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Truly, it is incredible...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:33.34,0:12:36.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}the way that Wonkamania\Nhas descended upon the globe.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.59,0:12:39.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}While the world searches,\Nwe watch and wait...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.55,0:12:41.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}wondering where the pursuit will lead...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.76,0:12:45.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and how long the spirit of man will hold up\Nunder the strain.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:45.18,0:12:49.43,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm still having these dreams, Doctor,\Nand I still can't stop believing them.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.52,0:12:51.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I've told you, Mr. Hoffstedder...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.56,0:12:54.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}to believe in one's dreams\Nis a manifestation of insanity.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.94,0:12:58.07,Default,,0,0,0,,The sooner you accept this,\Nthe sooner you'll get well.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:58.15,0:13:01.28,Default,,0,0,0,,But I dreamed the archangel appeared\Nand whispered into my ear...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.37,0:13:03.62,Default,,0,0,0,,and told me where to find\Na Golden Wonka Ticket.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:03.70,0:13:05.29,Default,,0,0,0,,What exactly did he say?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.37,0:13:08.75,Default,,0,0,0,,What difference does that make?\NThis was a dream, a fantasy.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.83,0:13:11.75,Default,,0,0,0,,HOFFSTEDDER: You said-\NDOCTOR: Just tell me where the ticket is!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.17,0:13:14.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We began with five Golden Tickets.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.21,0:13:18.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Like five lucky bolts of lightning\Nready to strike at any point on the map.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:19.05,0:13:22.01,Default,,0,0,0,,No one knew where or when\Nthe first one would hit.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:22.09,0:13:24.97,Default,,0,0,0,,But as you all know,\Nlast night we got our answer.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.06,0:13:28.40,Default,,0,0,0,,STANLEY: While we in America slept,\Nthe first Golden Ticket was found...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.48,0:13:31.48,Default,,0,0,0,,in the small town of Duselheim, Germany.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.56,0:13:34.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We've been waiting several hours\Nfor the follow-up story.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:34.57,0:13:36.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We're finally ready with a live report.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.94,0:13:39.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Proud we are,\Nfor the attention of the entire world...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.99,0:13:42.20,Default,,0,0,0,,focuses today right here in Duselheim.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:42.28,0:13:44.87,Default,,0,0,0,,A community suddenly thrust\Ninto prominence...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.95,0:13:48.87,Default,,0,0,0,,by the unexpected discovery\Nof the first Wonka Golden Ticket.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.04,0:13:52.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Its lucky finder is the son\Nof a most prominent butcher.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.21,0:13:54.92,Default,,0,0,0,,The boy's name, Augustus Gloop.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.55,0:14:00.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The pride of Duselheim,\Nthe fame of Western Germany.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.38,0:14:03.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}An example for the whole world.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.30,0:14:06.14,Default,,0,0,0,,REPORTER 2: How do you feel\Nto be the first Golden Ticket finder?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.22,0:14:08.22,Default,,0,0,0,,AUGUSTUS: Hungry.\NREPORTER 2: Any other feelings?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.31,0:14:11.69,Default,,0,0,0,,I feel sorry for Wonka.\NIt's gonna cost him a fortune in fudge.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:11.77,0:14:13.94,Default,,0,0,0,,REPORTER 1: Mr. Gloop,\Nwould you mind saying-
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.35,0:14:18.19,Default,,0,0,0,,REPORTER 2: Would you care to say\Na few words to the television audience?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.28,0:14:22.16,Default,,0,0,0,,I just knew Augustus would find\Na Golden Ticket. Eating is his hobby.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.24,0:14:23.33,Default,,0,0,0,,MRS. GLOOP: We encourage him.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.41,0:14:26.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He wouldn't do it\Nunless he needed the nourishment.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.53,0:14:28.70,Default,,0,0,0,,[Suspenseful instrumental music]
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.20,0:14:31.08,Default,,0,0,0,,ALL: Happy birthday, Charlie!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.00,0:14:35.59,Default,,0,0,0,,MRS. BUCKET: Here you are, Charlie.\NCHARLIE: Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.67,0:14:43.76,Default,,0,0,0,,It's terrific.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.84,0:14:47.22,Default,,0,0,0,,We each knitted a bit: Grandma Georgina,\NGrandma Josephine, and me.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.30,0:14:49.93,Default,,0,0,0,,I did the end pieces with the little tassels.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.02,0:14:53.36,Default,,0,0,0,,And here's a little gift\Nfrom Grandpa George and me.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.52,0:14:55.86,Default,,0,0,0,,I think I know what this is.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.86,0:15:01.11,Default,,0,0,0,,- It is. A Wonka.\N- Open it. Let's see that Golden Ticket.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.19,0:15:03.94,Default,,0,0,0,,- Wouldn't that be fantastic?\N- Don't raise his hopes.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.03,0:15:07.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Never mind. Go on, open it.\NI want to see that gold.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.20,0:15:08.41,Default,,0,0,0,,MRS. BUCKET: Stop it, Dad.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.49,0:15:10.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I've got the same chance as anybody else.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:10.49,0:15:11.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}GRANDPA: You've got more...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.04,0:15:13.75,Default,,0,0,0,,because you want it more.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.83,0:15:16.50,Default,,0,0,0,,- Go on, open it.\N- Here goes.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.84,0:15:21.59,Default,,0,0,0,,- I got it!\N- Where?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.67,0:15:22.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's see!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:23.01,0:15:26.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Fooled you, didn't I?\NYou thought I really had it.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:28.43,0:15:31.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Never mind, Charlie. You'll find one.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.02,0:15:36.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}- Here, everybody have a bite.\N- No.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.91,0:15:50.91,Default,,0,0,0,,VERUCA: I wanted to be the first\Nto find a Golden Ticket, Daddy.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.99,0:15:54.24,Default,,0,0,0,,MR. SALT: I know, angel.\NWe're doing the best we can.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.33,0:15:57.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I've got every girl on the bleeding staff\Nhunting for you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:15:57.42,0:15:59.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Then where is it?\NWhy haven't they found it?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.75,0:16:04.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}MR. SALT: Veruca, sweetheart,\NI'm not a magician. Give me time!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.76,0:16:08.01,Default,,0,0,0,,I want it now!\NWhat's the matter with those twerps?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.09,0:16:11.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}For five days now,\Nthe entire factory's been on the job!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.76,0:16:14.60,Default,,0,0,0,,They haven't shelled a peanut in there\Nsince Monday!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.68,0:16:18.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}They've been shelling\Nflaming chocolate bars from dawn to dusk!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.19,0:16:19.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Make them work nights.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:21.73,0:16:23.44,Default,,0,0,0,,MR. SALT: Come along, you girls!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.53,0:16:26.83,Default,,0,0,0,,MR. SALT: Put a jerk in it, or you'll be out\Non your ears, all of you!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.90,0:16:30.15,Default,,0,0,0,,And listen to this,\Nthe first girl that finds a Golden Ticket...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.24,0:16:33.33,Default,,0,0,0,,gets a �1 bonus in their pay packet!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.41,0:16:35.20,Default,,0,0,0,,What do you think of that?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.29,0:16:36.83,Default,,0,0,0,,[Girls cheering]
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.91,0:16:38.41,Default,,0,0,0,,VERUCA: They're not even trying.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.50,0:16:41.34,Default,,0,0,0,,They don't want to find it.\NThey're jealous of me.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.42,0:16:43.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Sweetheart, I can't push them no harder.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:43.75,0:16:46.17,Default,,0,0,0,,19,000 bars an hour they're shelling.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.26,0:16:50.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}MR. SALT: 760,000 they've done so far.\NVERUCA: You promised, Daddy.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.09,0:16:52.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You promised I'd have it the very first day!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.01,0:16:57.06,Default,,0,0,0,,You're going to be very unpopular, Henry,\Nif you don't deliver soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.14,0:17:00.52,Default,,0,0,0,,It breaks my heart, Henrietta.\NI hate to see her unhappy.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.60,0:17:02.27,Default,,0,0,0,,I won't talk to you ever again.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.36,0:17:05.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You're a rotten, mean father!\NYou never give me anything I want!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.86,0:17:10.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}- I won't go to school till I have it.\N- Veruca, sweetheart, angel.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.57,0:17:13.32,Default,,0,0,0,,There are only four tickets left\Nin the whole world...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.41,0:17:17.50,Default,,0,0,0,,and the whole world's hunting for them!\NWhat can I do?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.58,0:17:20.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I've got it, Mr. Salt! Here it is!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.79,0:17:25.38,Default,,0,0,0,,VERUCA: About time, too! I want it!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.46,0:17:27.05,Default,,0,0,0,,[Cheering]
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.63,0:17:33.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}VERUCA: Give me that ticket! It's mine!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.80,0:17:36.30,Default,,0,0,0,,I found a Golden Ticket!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.52,0:17:38.69,Default,,0,0,0,,[Suspenseful instrumental music]
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.81,0:17:43.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank God.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.40,0:17:48.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Happiness is what counts with children.\NHappiness and harmony.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.86,0:17:53.99,Default,,0,0,0,,REPORTER: This is the sign of our times.\NThe symbol of the havoc...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.07,0:17:56.91,Default,,0,0,0,,the mad craze\Nthat's sweeping the world today.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:56.99,0:18:01.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Whatever corner of the globe we are in,\Nwhichever continent we're on...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.33,0:18:05.21,Default,,0,0,0,,the great search for Wonka Bars\Ncontinues. We're nearing the end...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.29,0:18:07.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}of our 43rd day\Nin the hunt for Golden Tickets.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:08.76,0:18:11.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And everywhere,\Nwe're beginning to see signs of anxiety.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.80,0:18:13.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Every hour on the hour...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:13.43,0:18:16.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}new shipments are being sent\Nto points around the globe.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:16.43,0:18:18.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But they're just not moving fast enough.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.68,0:18:23.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}As time passes, the men who seek them\Nbecome more and more desperate.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.27,0:18:26.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}COMPUTER EXPERT: Gentlemen,\NI know how anxious you've been...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:26.11,0:18:27.53,Default,,0,0,0,,during these last few days.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:27.61,0:18:29.99,Default,,0,0,0,,But now I think I can safely say...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.19,0:18:33.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}that your time and money\Nhave been well-spent.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.20,0:18:36.95,Default,,0,0,0,,We're about to witness\Nthe greatest miracle of the Machine Age.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.16,0:18:40.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Based on the revolutionary\Nlaw of probability...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:40.25,0:18:43.88,Default,,0,0,0,,this machine will tell us\Nthe precise location...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.96,0:18:47.09,Default,,0,0,0,,of the three remaining Golden Tickets.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.01,0:19:00.06,Default,,0,0,0,,It says,\N" I won't tell. That would be cheating. "
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.48,0:19:08.73,Default,,0,0,0,,I am now telling the computer...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:08.82,0:19:13.03,Default,,0,0,0,,that if it will tell me the correct answer,\NI will gladly share with it...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:13.11,0:19:14.86,Default,,0,0,0,,the grand prize.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.33,0:19:20.46,Default,,0,0,0,,He says:
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.54,0:19:24.63,Default,,0,0,0,," What would a computer do\Nwith a lifetime supply of chocolate?"
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.08,0:19:26.37,Default,,0,0,0,,[Laughing sheepishly]
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.42,0:19:33.97,Default,,0,0,0,,I am now telling the computer\Nexactly what he can do with the chocolate.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.76,0:19:40.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}TV ANNOUNCER: It can happen\Nright here, too, unbelievable as it sounds...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.18,0:19:41.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}right here in America.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:41.89,0:19:46.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Where even in the smallest town,\Nthe happiest of dreams can come true.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.81,0:19:48.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Because, folks, here she is.:{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:48.52,0:19:52.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Miss Violet Beauregarde,\Nfinder of Golden Ticket number three.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:52.36,0:19:54.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}From Miles City, Montana.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:54.11,0:19:55.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And with her, the proud parents.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:55.86,0:19:58.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Mr. Beauregarde,\Na prominent local politician, a civic leader.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:19:59.07,0:20:01.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Sam Beauregarde,\N'"Square Deal'" Sam to you...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:01.62,0:20:03.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}with today's great giveaway bargains.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.79,0:20:06.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The finest values you'll get\Nin the entire country.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:06.37,0:20:08.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}SAM: This number here-\NVIOLET: They don't want you!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.71,0:20:10.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}- Care to say a few words?\N- Sure I will.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:10.79,0:20:13.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Here is Golden Ticket number three,\Nand it's all mine.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:13.34,0:20:14.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}TV ANNOUNCER: Tell us how it happened.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:14.92,0:20:17.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'm a gum chewer,\Nbut when I heard about these tickets...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:17.97,0:20:20.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I laid off gum\Nand switched to candy bars instead.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.97,0:20:23.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Now, of course, I'm right back on gum.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:23.14,0:20:26.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I chew all day, except at meals,\Nwhen I stick it behind my ear.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.31,0:20:27.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}MOTHER: Violet.\NVIOLET: Cool it, Mother.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.02,0:20:32.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}This is a piece of gum I've been chewing\Non for three months solid. A world record.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:32.86,0:20:36.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It's beaten the record\Nheld by my best friend, Cornelia...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.28,0:20:38.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and was she mad.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:38.20,0:20:39.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Cornelia, how are you, sweetie?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:40.07,0:20:43.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Let me just butt in to say\Nif any of you folks watching...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:20:43.29,0:20:45.96,Default,,0,0,0,,[Suspenseful instrumental music]
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.63,0:20:52.96,Default,,0,0,0,,[Doorbell rings]
Dialogue: 0,0:20:53.80,0:20:55.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Charlie, what are you doing here?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:55.67,0:20:58.01,Default,,0,0,0,,I thought if you were ready,\NI'd walk you home.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:58.09,0:21:01.34,Default,,0,0,0,,I wish I were. Looks like\NI'm going to be here late tonight.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:01.43,0:21:05.64,Default,,0,0,0,,CHARLIE: Then I guess I'll be going.\NMRS. BUCKET: Stay for a minute.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:05.89,0:21:08.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Here. Pull up a pile of clothes\Nand sit down.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:11.56,0:21:13.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Everything all right at school?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:13.44,0:21:15.23,Default,,0,0,0,,CHARLIE: Yep.\NMRS. BUCKET: Good.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.40,0:21:18.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Go on your newspaper route today?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.36,0:21:20.61,Default,,0,0,0,,CHARLIE: Just finished.\NMRS. BUCKET: Good.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:23.28,0:21:25.37,Default,,0,0,0,,I wanted to tell you something.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:28.21,0:21:31.38,Default,,0,0,0,,CHARLIE: They found the third ticket today.\NMRS. BUCKET: Did they?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.88,0:21:36.88,Default,,0,0,0,,I guess I'll be going now.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:38.13,0:21:39.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Is that all?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.55,0:21:42.51,Default,,0,0,0,,I thought you'd like to know.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:42.64,0:21:46.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Most people are pretty interested.\NI know I'm interested.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:46.47,0:21:49.81,Default,,0,0,0,,There are only two tickets left, you know.\NJust two.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:49.89,0:21:51.60,Default,,0,0,0,,CHARLIE: Pretty soon, just one.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:51.69,0:21:53.73,Default,,0,0,0,,I wonder who the lucky ones will be.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:53.81,0:21:56.15,Default,,0,0,0,,In case you're wondering, it won't be me.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:56.23,0:21:59.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Just in case you're wondering,\Nyou can count me out.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:00.20,0:22:02.66,Default,,0,0,0,,There are 100 billion people in this world...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:02.74,0:22:05.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}and only five will find Golden Tickets.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:05.87,0:22:09.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Even if you had a sackful of money,\Nyou probably wouldn't find one.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:09.50,0:22:14.26,Default,,0,0,0,,After this is over, you'll be no different\Nfrom billions of others who didn't find one.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:14.33,0:22:17.38,Default,,0,0,0,,But I am different.\NI want it more than any of them.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:18.30,0:22:21.55,Default,,0,0,0,,You'll get your chance.\NOne day things will change.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:21.76,0:22:24.10,Default,,0,0,0,,When? When will they change?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:24.34,0:22:26.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Probably when you least expect it.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:29.93,0:22:31.18,Default,,0,0,0,,See you later.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:38.53,0:22:40.91,Default,,0,0,0,,[Melancholic instrumental music]
Dialogue: 0,0:22:44.66,0:22:49.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Singing] You get blue like everyone{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:49.70,0:22:53.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But me and Grandpa Joe{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:53.08,0:22:56.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Can make your troubles go away{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:57.75,0:22:59.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Blow away{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:00.96,0:23:04.17,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}There they go{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:05.55,0:23:07.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Cheer up, Charlie{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:09.01,0:23:11.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Give me a smile{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:12.06,0:23:16.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What happened to that smile\NI used to know?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:18.73,0:23:20.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Don't you know your grin{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:21.07,0:23:24.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Has always been my sunshine{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:25.70,0:23:30.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Let that sunshine show{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:31.87,0:23:34.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Come on, Charlie{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:35.67,0:23:38.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}No need to frown{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:38.84,0:23:40.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Deep down you know{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.84,0:23:44.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The world is still your toy{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:45.84,0:23:48.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}When the world gets heavy{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:48.51,0:23:51.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Never pit-a-pat 'em{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:52.18,0:23:56.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Up and at 'em, boy{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:23:58.27,0:24:03.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Someday, sweet as a song{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:03.86,0:24:08.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Charlie's lucky day will come along{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:10.45,0:24:15.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Till that day\NYou've got to stay strong, Charlie{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:17.21,0:24:22.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Up on top is right where you belong{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:24.38,0:24:27.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Look up, Charlie{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:28.14,0:24:31.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You'll see a star{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:31.31,0:24:36.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Just follow it\NAnd keep your dream in view{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:38.65,0:24:44.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Pretty soon the sky\Nis gonna clear up, Charlie{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:45.90,0:24:49.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Cheer up, Charlie, do{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:52.49,0:24:55.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Cheer up, Charlie{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:24:57.12,0:25:03.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Just be glad you're you{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:09.13,0:25:10.01,Default,,0,0,0,,[Gunshots on TV]
Dialogue: 0,0:25:10.09,0:25:12.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}NEWSCASTER: While the rest of the world\Nsearches...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:12.35,0:25:14.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}here in the Southwest,\Nit has actually happened.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:14.60,0:25:18.69,Default,,0,0,0,,That's what I said. There's only\None Golden Ticket left in the entire world.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:18.77,0:25:22.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Because right here, in our own community\Nof Marble Falls, Arizona...
Dialogue: 0,0:25:22.52,0:25:24.44,Default,,0,0,0,,is lucky winner number four.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:24.53,0:25:28.49,Default,,0,0,0,,The name soon to be heard\Naround the universe is Mr. Mike Teevee.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:28.57,0:25:30.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Can we shut that thing off?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:30.36,0:25:31.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you crazy?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:31.66,0:25:33.29,Default,,0,0,0,,MRS. TEEVEE: He'll answer\Nduring the break.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:33.37,0:25:35.66,Default,,0,0,0,,NEWSCASTER: The country\Nwants to hear from you.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:35.74,0:25:37.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Can't you shut up? I'm busy.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:37.96,0:25:39.21,Default,,0,0,0,,What a great show.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:39.29,0:25:42.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I serve all his TV dinners right here.\NHe's never even been to the table.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:43.00,0:25:44.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}- You love to watch TV?\N- You bet.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:25:44.96,0:25:48.30,Default,,0,0,0,,- What about that Golden Ticket-\N- Hold it. I want to catch this.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:48.38,0:25:49.63,Default,,0,0,0,,REPORTER 1: Like the killings?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:49.72,0:25:51.47,Default,,0,0,0,,What do you think life's all about?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:51.55,0:25:53.80,Default,,0,0,0,,REPORTER 2: Mike, would you tell us if-
Dialogue: 0,0:25:54.97,0:25:57.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait till I get a real one. Colt.45.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:57.98,0:26:02.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}- Pop won't let me have one yet, will you?\N- Not till you're 12, Son.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:04.77,0:26:07.15,Default,,0,0,0,,[Suspenseful instrumental music]
Dialogue: 0,0:26:08.90,0:26:10.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Four down, one to go.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:10.99,0:26:15.12,Default,,0,0,0,,And somewhere out there,\Nanother lucky person is moving closer...
Dialogue: 0,0:26:15.33,0:26:19.79,Default,,0,0,0,,to finding the last\Nof the most sought-after prizes in history.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:20.41,0:26:23.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Though we cannot help but envy him,\Nwhoever he is...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:23.42,0:26:26.51,Default,,0,0,0,,and we might be tempted\Nto be bitter at our losing...
Dialogue: 0,0:26:26.59,0:26:29.51,Default,,0,0,0,,we must remember\Nthere are many more important things.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:29.59,0:26:32.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Many more important things.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:32.59,0:26:36.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Offhand, I can't think of what they are,\Nbut I'm sure there must be something.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:36.60,0:26:38.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Now for tomorrow's weather and...
Dialogue: 0,0:26:40.14,0:26:43.44,Default,,0,0,0,,CHARLIE: Why did you wake me up,\NGrandpa? Is something wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:49.61,0:26:51.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Grandpa, that money was for tobacco.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:52.07,0:26:55.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I told you, I've given it up. Go on, open it.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:26:55.95,0:27:00.00,Default,,0,0,0,,- One ticket left. Let's see that gold.\N- No, you do it. I can't.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:01.25,0:27:03.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Something tells me\Nwe're going to be lucky this time.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:04.04,0:27:06.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I've got a funny feeling inside.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:27:08.30,0:27:10.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Which end shall I open first?
Dialogue: 0,0:27:11.80,0:27:14.01,Default,,0,0,0,,That end. Just a tiny bit.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:15.64,0:27:18.23,Default,,0,0,0,,- Like this?\N- Now a bit more.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:19.39,0:27:22.39,Default,,0,0,0,,- You finish it. I can't.\N- No, Grandpa. You do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:22.81,0:27:25.56,Default,,0,0,0,,All right. Here goes.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:32.24,0:27:33.66,Default,,0,0,0,,You know...
Dialogue: 0,0:27:34.57,0:27:38.57,Default,,0,0,0,,I bet those Golden Tickets\Nmake the chocolate taste terrible.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:44.92,0:27:46.46,Default,,0,0,0,,[People chattering]
Dialogue: 0,0:27:49.29,0:27:50.92,Default,,0,0,0,,AUCTIONEER: Lot 403.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:51.00,0:27:53.55,Default,,0,0,0,,I can personally guarantee,\Nladies and gentlemen...
Dialogue: 0,0:27:53.63,0:27:57.43,Default,,0,0,0,,that this is the one and only,\Nthe absolutely last case of Wonka Bars...
Dialogue: 0,0:27:57.51,0:27:59.30,Default,,0,0,0,,left in the United Kingdom.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:59.39,0:28:03.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Shall we start the bidding at �1,000?\NDo I hear �1,000?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:03.81,0:28:08.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}�1,500. �2,000. I have �2,500 here.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:08.27,0:28:12.73,Default,,0,0,0,,�4,000. �4,500. �5,000...
Dialogue: 0,0:28:13.28,0:28:14.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:18.45,0:28:20.12,Default,,0,0,0,,DETECTIVE: I'm sorry, Mrs. Curtis.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:20.20,0:28:22.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}There's nothing in these papers\Nto give us a clue.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:22.79,0:28:24.96,Default,,0,0,0,,They kidnapped my husband 12 hours ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:25.04,0:28:27.33,Default,,0,0,0,,When will we hear from them?\NWhat do they want?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:27.42,0:28:31.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Try to stay calm. They did it for ransom.\NWe must wait to hear their demands.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:31.46,0:28:33.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'll give them anything they want.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:33.88,0:28:35.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}All I want is to have Harold back.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:36.05,0:28:37.59,Default,,0,0,0,,[Phone ringing]
Dialogue: 0,0:28:41.14,0:28:42.93,Default,,0,0,0,,DETECTIVE: Go ahead, we're listening.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:48.23,0:28:51.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What did they asked for?\NWhatever it is, they can have it.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:28:51.73,0:28:54.23,Default,,0,0,0,,They want your case of Wonka Bars.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:59.66,0:29:01.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Did you hear me?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:01.99,0:29:05.41,Default,,0,0,0,,It's your husband's life\Nor your case of Wonka Bars.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:06.08,0:29:08.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}How long will they give me\Nto think it over?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:10.00,0:29:13.75,Default,,0,0,0,,That's it, it's all over.\NThe Wonka contest is all over.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:13.84,0:29:16.01,Default,,0,0,0,,The fifth and final ticket has been found.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:16.09,0:29:20.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We've got a live report coming in\Ndirectly from Paraguay, South America.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:20.68,0:29:23.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Ladies and gentlemen, it is finished.\NThe end has come.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:23.35,0:29:26.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The fifth and last Golden Ticket\Nhas just been found...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:26.27,0:29:27.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}right here in Paraguay.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:27.85,0:29:30.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The finder is lucky Alberto Minoleta...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:31.02,0:29:34.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}the multimillionaire owner of gambling\Ncasinos throughout South America.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:35.03,0:29:38.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Here is the most recent picture available\Nof the happy finder.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:38.57,0:29:41.28,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}- The man who has finally...\N- Turn it off.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:29:42.70,0:29:44.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, that's that.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:44.87,0:29:48.79,Default,,0,0,0,,- No more Golden Tickets.\N- A lot of rubbish, the whole thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:48.87,0:29:50.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Not to Charlie, it wasn't.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:50.54,0:29:55.34,Default,,0,0,0,,A little boy needs something to hope for.\NWhat's he got to hope for now?
Dialogue: 0,0:29:55.55,0:29:57.64,Default,,0,0,0,,GEORGINA: Who's going to tell him?
Dialogue: 0,0:29:57.76,0:30:00.89,Default,,0,0,0,,MRS. BUCKET: Let's not wake him.\NHe'll find out soon enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:00.97,0:30:04.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}GRANDPA: Yeah, let him sleep.\NLet him have one last dream.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:06.22,0:30:07.81,Default,,0,0,0,,[Slow instrumental music]
Dialogue: 0,0:30:10.77,0:30:12.61,Default,,0,0,0,,[Turkentine clearing throat]
Dialogue: 0,0:30:12.81,0:30:15.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I've just decided to switch\Nour Friday's schedule to Monday.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:15.82,0:30:19.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Which means Friday's test\Non what we learned during the week...
Dialogue: 0,0:30:19.49,0:30:22.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}will now take place on Monday\Nbefore we've learned it.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:30:22.16,0:30:24.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Since today's Tuesday,\Nit doesn't matter in the slightest.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:24.99,0:30:26.74,Default,,0,0,0,,TURKENTINE: Pencils ready.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:28.16,0:30:31.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Today we are going to learn about...
Dialogue: 0,0:30:32.54,0:30:33.67,Default,,0,0,0,,percentages.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:33.75,0:30:37.38,Default,,0,0,0,,For example, let's take\Nthe recent unpleasantness.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:37.59,0:30:40.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Supposing that there were\N1,000 Wonka Bars in the world...
Dialogue: 0,0:30:40.88,0:30:44.68,Default,,0,0,0,,and during the contest you each opened\Na certain number of them.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:44.85,0:30:47.02,Default,,0,0,0,,That number is...
Dialogue: 0,0:30:47.56,0:30:49.73,Default,,0,0,0,,a percent. Everyone understand?
Dialogue: 0,0:30:49.81,0:30:51.35,Default,,0,0,0,,[Students moaning]
Dialogue: 0,0:30:51.44,0:30:54.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Madeline Durkin,\Nhow many Wonka Bars did you open?
Dialogue: 0,0:30:54.61,0:30:55.86,Default,,0,0,0,,About 100.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:55.94,0:31:00.74,Default,,0,0,0,,There are ten 100s in 1,000.\NTherefore, you opened 10%.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:01.36,0:31:03.78,Default,,0,0,0,,Peter Goff, how many did you open?
Dialogue: 0,0:31:03.86,0:31:05.45,Default,,0,0,0,,One hundred and fifty.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:05.53,0:31:09.28,Default,,0,0,0,,That's 10% half over again,\Nwhich makes 15%.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:09.54,0:31:12.84,Default,,0,0,0,,- Charlie Bucket, how many did you open?\N- Two.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:12.96,0:31:17.17,Default,,0,0,0,,- That's easy. 200 is twice-\N- Not 200.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:17.71,0:31:19.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Just two.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:19.38,0:31:22.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Two? What do you mean,\Nyou only opened two?
Dialogue: 0,0:31:22.63,0:31:24.72,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't care very much for chocolate.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:24.80,0:31:29.10,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't figure out just two.\NSo let's pretend you opened 200.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:29.22,0:31:33.52,Default,,0,0,0,,If you opened 200 Wonka Bars,\Napart from being dreadfully sick...
Dialogue: 0,0:31:33.60,0:31:35.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}you'd have used up 20% of 1,000...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:31:35.56,0:31:38.48,Default,,0,0,0,,which is 15% half over again, 10%...
Dialogue: 0,0:31:55.33,0:31:58.12,Default,,0,0,0,,[Mysterious instrumental music]
Dialogue: 0,0:32:06.22,0:32:08.76,Default,,0,0,0,,[Cheerful instrumental music]
Dialogue: 0,0:32:25.86,0:32:27.36,Default,,0,0,0,,[Charlie clearing throat]
Dialogue: 0,0:32:28.07,0:32:31.20,Default,,0,0,0,,CHARLIE: I'd like a bar of chocolate, please.\NBILL: Sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:31.58,0:32:32.79,Default,,0,0,0,,What kind?
Dialogue: 0,0:32:32.87,0:32:35.96,Default,,0,0,0,,A Slugworth Sizzler?\NA Wonka Scrumdiddleumptious?
Dialogue: 0,0:32:36.04,0:32:39.67,Default,,0,0,0,,- Whichever is biggest.\N- Try the Wonka Scrumdiddleumptious.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:39.92,0:32:44.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Now that the tickets have been found,\NI don't have to hide them anymore.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:32:47.63,0:32:49.22,Default,,0,0,0,,[Bill clearing throat]
Dialogue: 0,0:32:56.06,0:32:57.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Take it easy.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:57.64,0:33:00.31,Default,,0,0,0,,You'll get a stomachache\Nif you swallow it like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:00.40,0:33:02.28,Default,,0,0,0,,- Bye.\N- Bye, now.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:10.07,0:33:13.41,Default,,0,0,0,,I think I'll buy just one more,\Nfor my Grandpa Joe.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:13.62,0:33:14.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:15.66,0:33:18.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Why not try\Na regular Wonka Bar this time?
Dialogue: 0,0:33:18.08,0:33:19.42,Default,,0,0,0,,CHARLIE: Fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:23.59,0:33:25.18,Default,,0,0,0,,[People talking excitedly]
Dialogue: 0,0:33:27.51,0:33:30.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}MR. JOPECK: Hear about the scandal.\NMAN 1: Give me a newspaper.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:30.55,0:33:32.22,Default,,0,0,0,,MR. JOPECK: All right.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:32.30,0:33:35.64,Default,,0,0,0,,MR. JOPECK: Take it easy. One at a time.\NMAN 2: Did you hear the news?
Dialogue: 0,0:33:35.72,0:33:38.10,Default,,0,0,0,,MAN 3: That gambler from Paraguay\Nmade a phony ticket.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:38.19,0:33:41.44,Default,,0,0,0,,MAN 2: That means there's\None Golden Ticket still floating around.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:41.52,0:33:45.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}MAN 3: Can you imagine the nerve\Nof that guy? Trying to fool the whole world.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:33:45.32,0:33:49.16,Default,,0,0,0,,MAN 2: He really was a crook.\NThis means the contest goes on forever.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:02.04,0:34:04.50,Default,,0,0,0,,[Suspenseful instrumental music]
Dialogue: 0,0:34:23.98,0:34:26.90,Default,,0,0,0,,[Triumphant instrumental music]
Dialogue: 0,0:34:32.41,0:34:35.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You've got it!\NYou've got the last Golden Ticket!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:35.20,0:34:38.04,Default,,0,0,0,,The kid's found the last Golden Ticket!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:39.45,0:34:40.99,Default,,0,0,0,,MAN 4: It really is gold.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:41.08,0:34:44.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}MR. JOPECK: Stand back. Leave him alone.\NWOMAN: Let me see.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:44.21,0:34:46.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}MR. JOPECK: You'll kill him.\NLeave him alone.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:34:46.34,0:34:48.84,Default,,0,0,0,,MR. JOPECK: Break it up!\NMAN 5: Show it over here.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:48.92,0:34:51.46,Default,,0,0,0,,MR. JOPECK: Come on, Charlie.\NHold on to the ticket.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:51.55,0:34:55.97,Default,,0,0,0,,MR. JOPECK: Run for it! Run straight home,\Nand don't stop till you get there!
Dialogue: 0,0:34:56.14,0:34:58.60,Default,,0,0,0,,[Fast-paced instrumental music]
Dialogue: 0,0:35:25.42,0:35:27.71,Default,,0,0,0,,[Ominous instrumental music]
Dialogue: 0,0:35:27.92,0:35:30.96,Default,,0,0,0,,I congratulate you, little boy. Well done.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:31.42,0:35:33.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You've found the fifth Golden Ticket.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:35:34.09,0:35:37.34,Default,,0,0,0,,May I introduce myself? Arthur Slugworth.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:37.93,0:35:40.72,Default,,0,0,0,,President of Slugworth Chocolates, Inc.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:41.31,0:35:45.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Listen carefully,\Nbecause I'm going to make you very rich.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:45.44,0:35:49.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Mr. Wonka is at this moment\Nworking on a fantastic invention.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:49.65,0:35:51.94,Default,,0,0,0,,The Everlasting Gobstopper.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:52.61,0:35:54.74,Default,,0,0,0,,If he succeeds, he'll ruin me.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:54.82,0:35:58.24,Default,,0,0,0,,So I want you to get hold of\Njust one Everlasting Gobstopper...
Dialogue: 0,0:35:58.33,0:36:01.92,Default,,0,0,0,,and bring it to me\Nso that I can find the secret formula.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:02.00,0:36:05.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Your reward will be 10,000 of these.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:05.79,0:36:09.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Think it over, will you?\NA new house for your family...
Dialogue: 0,0:36:09.84,0:36:13.13,Default,,0,0,0,,and good food and comfort\Nfor the rest of their lives.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:13.97,0:36:15.89,Default,,0,0,0,,And don't forget the name:
Dialogue: 0,0:36:15.97,0:36:18.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Everlasting Gobstopper.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:27.81,0:36:30.52,Default,,0,0,0,,[Cheerful instrumental music]
Dialogue: 0,0:36:47.62,0:36:51.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Look, everybody!\NI've got it! The fifth Golden Ticket is mine!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:36:51.38,0:36:55.97,Default,,0,0,0,,You're pulling our legs, Charlie.\NThere aren't any more Golden Tickets.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:56.05,0:36:59.30,Default,,0,0,0,,No, Grandpa, the last one was a fake.\NIt said so in the papers.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:59.39,0:37:02.98,Default,,0,0,0,,I found some money, bought a Wonka Bar,\Nand the ticket was in it!
Dialogue: 0,0:37:03.06,0:37:05.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Look at it. See for yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:06.06,0:37:08.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Read it, Joe, for heaven's sake.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:09.06,0:37:13.36,Default,,0,0,0,," Greetings to you,\Nthe lucky finder of this Golden Ticket...
Dialogue: 0,0:37:13.57,0:37:17.66,Default,,0,0,0,," from Mr. Willy Wonka.\NPresent this ticket at the factory gates...
Dialogue: 0,0:37:17.74,0:37:21.99,Default,,0,0,0,," at 10:00 in the morning on October 1,\Nand do not be late.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:22.20,0:37:27.00,Default,,0,0,0,," You may bring with you one member\Nof your own family, but no one else.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:27.21,0:37:30.34,Default,,0,0,0,," In your wildest dreams,\Nyou could not imagine...
Dialogue: 0,0:37:30.42,0:37:33.13,Default,,0,0,0,," the marvelous surprises that await you. "
Dialogue: 0,0:37:33.21,0:37:36.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}GRANDPA: Charlie, you've done it!\NMRS. BUCKET: I can't believe it.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:37:37.22,0:37:41.27,Default,,0,0,0,,It says I can take somebody with me.\NI wish you could go.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:59.07,0:38:00.15,Default,,0,0,0,,[Grandpa groans]
Dialogue: 0,0:38:00.24,0:38:03.41,Default,,0,0,0,,That's good, Charlie. Now help me up.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:17.26,0:38:20.64,Default,,0,0,0,,CHARLIE: Are you okay?\NGRANDPA: I'm fine, Charlie.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:25.85,0:38:26.93,Default,,0,0,0,,[Charlie exclaiming]
Dialogue: 0,0:38:27.02,0:38:28.02,Default,,0,0,0,,MRS. BUCKET: Easy, Dad.\NJOSEPHINE: Joe!
Dialogue: 0,0:38:30.64,0:38:32.14,Default,,0,0,0,,JOSEPHINE: Watch it, Joe.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:41.32,0:38:42.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Look at me.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:45.70,0:38:47.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Look at me!
Dialogue: 0,0:38:48.33,0:38:50.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Up and about.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:51.96,0:38:55.59,Default,,0,0,0,,I haven't done this in 20 years.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:56.38,0:38:57.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Grandpa.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:01.80,0:39:05.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Singing] I never thought my life could be{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:06.81,0:39:10.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Anything but catastrophe{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:11.48,0:39:15.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But suddenly I begin to see{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:15.81,0:39:20.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}A bit of good luck for me{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:20.82,0:39:24.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}'Cause I've got a Golden Ticket{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:26.41,0:39:32.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I've got a golden twinkle in my eye{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:36.67,0:39:39.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I never had a chance to shine{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:39.63,0:39:41.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Never a happy song to sing{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:41.88,0:39:43.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But suddenly half the world is mine{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:44.01,0:39:45.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What an amazing thing!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:45.80,0:39:47.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}'Cause I've got a Golden Ticket{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:47.85,0:39:49.64,Default,,0,0,0,,It's ours, Charlie.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:49.85,0:39:53.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Singing] I've got a golden sun up in the sky{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:39:53.69,0:39:55.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Slippers, Charlie.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:55.90,0:39:57.65,Default,,0,0,0,,[Lively instrumental music]
Dialogue: 0,0:39:57.73,0:40:01.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Singing] I never thought I'd see the day\NWhen I would face the world and say{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:01.40,0:40:04.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}GRANDPA AND CHARLIE: '"Good morning,\Nlook at the sun '"{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:05.07,0:40:08.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}GRANDPA: I never thought that I would be\NSlap in the lap of luxury{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:08.70,0:40:10.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Because I'd have said.:{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:10.58,0:40:12.12,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}CHARLIE: '"It couldn't be done'"{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:12.33,0:40:14.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}GRANDPA: But it can be done{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:15.67,0:40:17.67,Default,,0,0,0,,The cane, Charlie.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:20.71,0:40:22.34,Default,,0,0,0,,[Grandpa laughing]
Dialogue: 0,0:40:22.42,0:40:24.01,Default,,0,0,0,,GRANDPA: Here I go.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:24.93,0:40:26.77,Default,,0,0,0,,[Laughing] Watch my speed.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:32.06,0:40:33.27,Default,,0,0,0,,[Grandpa singing]
Dialogue: 0,0:40:33.35,0:40:37.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I never dreamed that I would climb\NOver the moon in ecstasy{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:37.10,0:40:40.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But nevertheless it's there\NThat I'm shortly about to be{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:40.82,0:40:43.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}GRANDPA AND CHARLIE:\N'Cause I've got a Golden Ticket{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:44.36,0:40:48.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I've got a golden chance to make my way{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:48.37,0:40:53.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And with a Golden Ticket, it's a golden day{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:40:56.58,0:40:58.83,Default,,0,0,0,,[Lively instrumental music continues]
Dialogue: 0,0:41:09.85,0:41:12.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Good morning! Look at the sun!
Dialogue: 0,0:41:17.14,0:41:20.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}GRANDPA AND CHARLIE: [Singing]\NBecause I'd have said it couldn't be done{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:21.23,0:41:23.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But it can be done{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:24.57,0:41:28.57,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I never dreamed that I would climb\NOver the moon in ecstasy{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:28.66,0:41:32.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But nevertheless it's there\NThat I'm shortly about to be{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:32.74,0:41:35.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}'Cause I've got a Golden Ticket{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:35.58,0:41:37.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}GRANDPA AND CHARLIE:\NI've got a Golden Ticket{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:37.66,0:41:41.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I've got a golden chance to make my way{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:41.50,0:41:46.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And with a Golden Ticket it's a golden day{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:50.34,0:41:53.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Stop! It says October 1. That's tomorrow.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:53.93,0:41:58.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We've got a lot to do. Comb your hair,\Nwash your face, polish your shoes-{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:41:58.31,0:42:00.15,Default,,0,0,0,,MRS. BUCKET: I'll take care of everything.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:00.23,0:42:01.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We don't have time.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:01.44,0:42:05.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Grandpa, on the way home today,\NI ran into Mr. Slugworth.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:07.53,0:42:10.03,Default,,0,0,0,,[Marching band\Ninstrumental music playing]
Dialogue: 0,0:42:30.30,0:42:32.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, Mom, we're on TV.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:32.22,0:42:34.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Hi, everybody in Marble Falls!
Dialogue: 0,0:42:34.39,0:42:38.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Hi, Billy. Hi, Maggie. Hi, Fishface.\NHow do I look?
Dialogue: 0,0:42:38.31,0:42:39.90,Default,,0,0,0,,ANNOUNCER: You guys ready?\NMAN: You're on.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:39.98,0:42:41.77,Default,,0,0,0,,This is the big day, folks.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:41.85,0:42:46.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The day Willy Wonka will open his gates\Nand shower gifts on the five lucky winners.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:46.82,0:42:50.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}From everywhere, people have gathered\Nwaiting for the hour to strike...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:42:50.82,0:42:54.49,Default,,0,0,0,,waiting to catch a glimpse\Nof that legendary magician, Willy Wonka.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:56.16,0:42:59.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Hi, Sam Beauregarde here. Don't forget\Nto visit Beauregarde's Auto Mart-
Dialogue: 0,0:42:59.87,0:43:02.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Cut it out, Dad!\NFor heaven's sake, this is my show.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:02.92,0:43:06.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Hi, Cornelia, sweetie. I've still got it.\NHow's this for a stretch?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:11.47,0:43:12.89,Default,,0,0,0,,[People chattering]
Dialogue: 0,0:43:19.93,0:43:24.27,Default,,0,0,0,,- I want to go in first before anybody else.\N- Anything you say, sweetheart.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:27.52,0:43:30.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Save some room for later,\NAugustus, Liebling.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:33.86,0:43:37.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Whispering] Grandpa, I don't believe it.\NWe did it. We're actually going in.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:43:37.78,0:43:41.53,Default,,0,0,0,,We're going to see\Nthe greatest of them all, Mr. Willy Wonka.
Dialogue: 0,0:43:41.79,0:43:43.88,Default,,0,0,0,,[Clock dinging]
Dialogue: 0,0:44:08.65,0:44:10.82,Default,,0,0,0,,[People cheering and applauding]
Dialogue: 0,0:45:17.59,0:45:19.63,Default,,0,0,0,,[People cheering]
Dialogue: 0,0:45:22.89,0:45:24.22,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:28.81,0:45:32.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Welcome, my friends.\NWelcome to my chocolate factory.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:32.98,0:45:35.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Would you come forward, please?
Dialogue: 0,0:45:35.40,0:45:38.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Get back, you.\NCome on, Veruca, sweetheart.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:39.32,0:45:41.24,Default,,0,0,0,,[Cheering]
Dialogue: 0,0:45:43.45,0:45:46.04,Default,,0,0,0,,[Whispering] That's Slugworth,\Nthe man I told you about.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:50.54,0:45:53.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}WONKA: Welcome.\NIt's nice to have you here.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:45:53.42,0:45:55.30,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm so glad you could come.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:55.38,0:45:59.30,Default,,0,0,0,,This is going to be such an exciting day.\NI hope you enjoy it.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:59.72,0:46:01.22,Default,,0,0,0,,I think you will.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:01.43,0:46:04.64,Default,,0,0,0,,And now would you please show me\Nyour Golden Tickets?
Dialogue: 0,0:46:04.81,0:46:06.31,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm Veruca Salt.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:06.39,0:46:08.52,Default,,0,0,0,,My dear Veruca, what a pleasure.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:08.60,0:46:12.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}- You look pretty in that lovely mink coat.\N- I've got three others at home.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:12.86,0:46:17.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Mr. Salt, overjoyed to see you, sir.\NWould you just step over there?
Dialogue: 0,0:46:17.40,0:46:20.70,Default,,0,0,0,,- Augustus Gloop.\N- Augustus, my dear boy.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:20.78,0:46:23.45,Default,,0,0,0,,How good to see you,\Nand in such fine shape.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:23.58,0:46:26.96,Default,,0,0,0,,This must be the radiant Mrs. Gloop.\NJust over there, dear lady.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:27.04,0:46:28.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Violet Beauregarde.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:28.46,0:46:30.92,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: Darling child.\NWelcome to Wonka's.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:31.00,0:46:34.34,Default,,0,0,0,,VIOLET: What kind of gum you got here?\NWONKA: Charming.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:34.42,0:46:37.59,Default,,0,0,0,,- Sam Beauregarde here.\N- My dear sir, what a genuine pleasure.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:37.67,0:46:40.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Any automotive needs, call on Sam.\NPhone number's on the card.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:46:40.93,0:46:43.02,Default,,0,0,0,," With Sam B., it's a guarantee. "
Dialogue: 0,0:46:44.10,0:46:45.73,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm Mike Teevee.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:45.81,0:46:49.02,Default,,0,0,0,,MIKE: Wham, you're dead!\NWONKA: Wonderful to meet you, Mike.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:49.10,0:46:50.89,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: Mrs. Teevee, how do you do?
Dialogue: 0,0:46:50.98,0:46:53.07,Default,,0,0,0,,- What an adorable boy you have.\N- Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:53.15,0:46:55.44,Default,,0,0,0,,- Just over there.\N- Charlie Bucket.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:55.52,0:47:00.11,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: I read about you in\Nthe papers. I'm happy for you. Who's this?
Dialogue: 0,0:47:00.20,0:47:03.16,Default,,0,0,0,,CHARLIE: My grandfather, Grandpa Joe.\NWONKA: Delighted to meet you.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:03.24,0:47:05.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Overjoyed. Enraptured. Entranced.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:05.37,0:47:07.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Are we ready? Yes. Good. In we go.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:08.45,0:47:10.95,Default,,0,0,0,,[Marching band instrumental music\Nresumes playing]
Dialogue: 0,0:47:43.99,0:47:46.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Hats, coats, galoshes over here.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:46.49,0:47:49.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But hurry, please.\NWe have so much time and so little to see.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:47:49.75,0:47:51.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait a minute. Strike that.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:51.91,0:47:54.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Reverse it. Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:55.88,0:47:59.59,Default,,0,0,0,,VIOLET: When do I get my chocolate?\NSAM: First take off your coat, Violet.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:59.67,0:48:02.26,Default,,0,0,0,,MIKE: Boy, what weird-looking\Ncoat hangers.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:02.51,0:48:03.59,Default,,0,0,0,,[Violet and Mike scream]
Dialogue: 0,0:48:03.68,0:48:08.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Little surprises around every corner,\Nbut nothing dangerous. Don't be alarmed.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:08.43,0:48:12.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}As soon as your outer vestments\Nare in hand, we'll begin.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:48:13.14,0:48:17.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, will the children kindly step up here.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:28.37,0:48:30.54,Default,,0,0,0,,VIOLET: Accidents? What kind\Nof accidents?
Dialogue: 0,0:48:30.62,0:48:33.12,Default,,0,0,0,,MRS. TEEVEE: I didn't know\Nwe had to sign for this tour.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:33.21,0:48:35.34,Default,,0,0,0,,VIOLET: I can't see what it says\Nin the bottom.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:35.42,0:48:37.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Violet, you first.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:37.54,0:48:39.88,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: Sign here.\NSAM: Hold it.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:39.96,0:48:42.34,Default,,0,0,0,,SAM: Let me through.\NViolet, don't sign anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:42.42,0:48:45.55,Default,,0,0,0,,- What's this all about?\N- Standard formal contract.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:45.63,0:48:49.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't talk to me about contracts,\NI use them myself. They're for suckers.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:49.56,0:48:52.81,Default,,0,0,0,,You wouldn't begrudge me\Na little protection? A drop?
Dialogue: 0,0:48:52.89,0:48:54.60,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't sign anything without my lawyer.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:54.69,0:48:56.48,Default,,0,0,0,,MR. SALT: Veruca\Ndon't sign anything, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:56.56,0:48:57.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Then she don't go in.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:57.73,0:48:59.23,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry. Rules of the house.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:59.31,0:49:01.69,Default,,0,0,0,,I want to go in. Don't you dare stop me.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:01.78,0:49:03.41,Default,,0,0,0,,MR. SALT: I'm only trying to help you.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:03.49,0:49:07.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Give me that pen.\NYou're always making things difficult.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:08.91,0:49:12.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Nicely handled, Veruca.\NShe's a girl who knows where she's going.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:13.37,0:49:15.83,Default,,0,0,0,,What's all that small print at the bottom?
Dialogue: 0,0:49:15.91,0:49:19.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If you have any problems,\Ndial information. Thank you for calling.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:22.25,0:49:24.92,Default,,0,0,0,,MRS. TEEVEE: I assume there's\Nan accident indemnity clause?
Dialogue: 0,0:49:25.01,0:49:26.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Never between friends.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:26.26,0:49:30.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Saw this in a movie once.\NA guy signed his wife's insurance policy.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:30.30,0:49:32.18,Default,,0,0,0,,- Then he bumped her off.\N- Clever.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:32.26,0:49:35.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}- What about me, Grandpa?\N- Sign away. We've got nothing to lose.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:49:35.98,0:49:37.61,Default,,0,0,0,,VERUCA: Let's go in. Come on.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:37.69,0:49:40.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Patience, little dear.\NEverything has to be in order.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:41.48,0:49:43.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Everyone signed? Yes?
Dialogue: 0,0:49:43.65,0:49:45.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Good. On we go.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:54.66,0:49:56.25,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: Ninety-nine...
Dialogue: 0,0:49:56.46,0:49:57.92,Default,,0,0,0,,forty-four...
Dialogue: 0,0:49:58.00,0:49:59.92,Default,,0,0,0,,100% pure.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:01.50,0:50:03.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Just through the other door, please.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:06.67,0:50:10.26,Default,,0,0,0,,MR. SALT: There's some mistake here.\NMIKE: There is no other door.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:10.51,0:50:14.35,Default,,0,0,0,,- There's no way out.\N- I know there's a door here someplace.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:14.85,0:50:18.31,Default,,0,0,0,,SAM: I don't like this, Wonka.\NMR. SALT: Is this a trick or something?
Dialogue: 0,0:50:18.44,0:50:22.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Mr. Wonka, help!\NI'm getting squashed. Save me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:22.19,0:50:24.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Is it my soul that calls upon my name?
Dialogue: 0,0:50:24.61,0:50:26.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Let me out or I'll scream!
Dialogue: 0,0:50:26.53,0:50:29.03,Default,,0,0,0,,- Somebody's touching me.\N- Now look here, Wonka!
Dialogue: 0,0:50:29.11,0:50:33.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Excuse me, questions will come at the end of the session.\NWe must press on. Come along.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:35.12,0:50:37.08,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: Here we are.\NSAM: Ugh, don't be a damn fool. Wonka!
Dialogue: 0,0:50:37.16,0:50:38.83,Default,,0,0,0,,That's the way we came in.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:38.91,0:50:41.04,Default,,0,0,0,,It is? Are you sure?
Dialogue: 0,0:50:41.21,0:50:43.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We've just come through there.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:50:43.67,0:50:45.26,Default,,0,0,0,,How do you like that?
Dialogue: 0,0:50:46.13,0:50:48.42,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: There we are.\NMR. SALT: What is this, Wonka?
Dialogue: 0,0:50:48.51,0:50:51.35,Default,,0,0,0,,- Some kind of funhouse?\N- Why? Having fun?
Dialogue: 0,0:50:51.43,0:50:55.52,Default,,0,0,0,,MRS. TEEVEE: I'm had enough!\NI'm not going in there.\NMR. BEAUREGARDE: Come on, Violet, we're getting out of here.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:55.60,0:50:59.10,Default,,0,0,0,,You can't get out backwards.\NYou got to go forwards to go back.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:59.18,0:51:00.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Better press on.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:01.69,0:51:04.28,Default,,0,0,0,,MIKE: The room is getting smaller.\NMRS. TEEVEE: No, it's not.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:04.36,0:51:07.03,Default,,0,0,0,,MRS. TEEVEE: He's getting bigger.\NMR. SALT: He's at it again.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:07.11,0:51:09.95,Default,,0,0,0,,VIOLET: Where's the chocolate?\NSAM: I doubt if there is any.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:10.03,0:51:12.41,Default,,0,0,0,,I doubt if any of us\Nwill get out of here alive.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:12.49,0:51:14.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, you should never never doubt\Nwhat nobody is sure about.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:15.08,0:51:17.37,Default,,0,0,0,,You're not squeezing me\Nthrough that tiny door.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:17.45,0:51:20.20,Default,,0,0,0,,You're off your nut.\NNo one can get through there.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:20.29,0:51:24.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}My dear friends, you are now\Nabout to enter the nerve center...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:51:24.96,0:51:27.21,Default,,0,0,0,,to the entire Wonka factory.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:28.13,0:51:31.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Inside this room,\Nall of my dreams become realities.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:32.13,0:51:34.63,Default,,0,0,0,,And some of my realities become dreams.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:34.72,0:51:38.47,Default,,0,0,0,,And almost everything you'll see\Nis eatable, edible.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:38.56,0:51:40.77,Default,,0,0,0,,I mean, you can eat almost everything.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:40.85,0:51:42.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Let me in, I'm starving.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:42.73,0:51:45.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't get overexcited.\NDon't lose your head, Augustus.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:45.94,0:51:47.57,Default,,0,0,0,,We wouldn't want anyone to lose that.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:49.82,0:51:50.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:51.15,0:51:52.94,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: Now, the combination.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:53.16,0:51:55.16,Default,,0,0,0,,This is a musical lock.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:55.24,0:51:57.49,Default,,0,0,0,,[Lively piano music playing]
Dialogue: 0,0:51:57.66,0:51:58.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Rachmaninoff.
Dialogue: 0,0:51:59.08,0:52:01.04,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: Ladies and gentlemen...
Dialogue: 0,0:52:01.50,0:52:03.17,Default,,0,0,0,,boys and girls...
Dialogue: 0,0:52:04.17,0:52:05.92,Default,,0,0,0,,the Chocolate Room.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:06.63,0:52:10.09,Default,,0,0,0,,[Suspenseful instrumental music]
Dialogue: 0,0:52:43.91,0:52:46.50,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: Hold your breath. Make a wish.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:46.75,0:52:48.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Count to three.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:48.96,0:52:52.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Singing] Come with me and you'll be{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:52.67,0:52:56.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}In a world of pure imagination{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:56.89,0:52:58.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Take a look{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:52:58.55,0:53:03.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And you'll see into your imagination{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:53:09.98,0:53:13.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We'll begin with a spin{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:53:14.19,0:53:17.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Traveling in the world of my creation{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:53:18.24,0:53:21.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What we'll see will defy{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:53:23.16,0:53:25.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Explanation{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:53:27.96,0:53:29.55,Default,,0,0,0,,[Slow instrumental music]
Dialogue: 0,0:53:35.80,0:53:39.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Singing] If you want to view paradise{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:53:39.64,0:53:42.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Simply look around and view it{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:53:44.02,0:53:47.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Anything you want to, do it{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:53:48.10,0:53:50.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Want to change the world{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:53:51.73,0:53:54.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}There's nothing to it{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:54:02.58,0:54:05.25,Default,,0,0,0,,SAM: Hurry up, Violet.\NCHARLIE: This way, Grandpa.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:12.13,0:54:14.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Singing] There is no life i know{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:54:15.05,0:54:18.22,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}To compare with pure imagination{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:54:18.30,0:54:21.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Living there you'll be free{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:54:21.60,0:54:25.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If you truly wish to be{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:06.64,0:55:10.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If you want to view paradise{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:10.69,0:55:13.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Simply look around and view it{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:14.31,0:55:17.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Anything you want to, do it{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:18.36,0:55:20.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Want to change the world{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:21.11,0:55:25.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}There's nothing to it{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:37.13,0:55:41.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}There is no life I know{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:42.55,0:55:47.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}To compare with pure imagination{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:48.81,0:55:53.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Living there you'll be free{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:55:55.40,0:55:58.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If you truly{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:00.82,0:56:04.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Wish to be{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:16.08,0:56:18.50,Default,,0,0,0,,MRS. GLOOP: What a disgusting,\Ndirty river.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:18.59,0:56:19.93,Default,,0,0,0,,It's industrial waste.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:20.01,0:56:22.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You've ruined your watershed, Wonka.\NIt's polluted.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:22.51,0:56:25.10,Default,,0,0,0,,- It's chocolate.\N- That's chocolate?
Dialogue: 0,0:56:25.18,0:56:26.52,Default,,0,0,0,,That's chocolate.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:26.60,0:56:28.19,Default,,0,0,0,,A chocolate river.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:28.26,0:56:30.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}GRANDPA: That's the most fantastic thing\NI've ever seen.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:30.68,0:56:32.52,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: 10,000 gallons an hour.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:32.77,0:56:36.52,Default,,0,0,0,,And look at my waterfall.\NThat's the most important thing.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:37.61,0:56:41.41,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It's mixing my chocolate.\NIt's actually churning my chocolate.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:56:41.61,0:56:45.36,Default,,0,0,0,,No other factory in the world\Nmixes its chocolate by waterfall.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:45.78,0:56:49.03,Default,,0,0,0,,But it's the only way\Nif you want it just right.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:49.20,0:56:53.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Grandpa, look over there across the river.\NThey're little men.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:53.12,0:56:55.04,Default,,0,0,0,,GRANDPA: Jumping crocodiles, Charlie!
Dialogue: 0,0:56:55.17,0:56:57.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Now we know who makes the chocolates.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:57.46,0:57:00.63,Default,,0,0,0,,MR. SALT: I never saw anybody\Nwith an orange face before.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:01.26,0:57:04.93,Default,,0,0,0,,MR. SALT: Aren't they funny-looking?\NMRS. TEEVEE: What are they doing there?
Dialogue: 0,0:57:05.01,0:57:06.97,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: Creaming and sugaring time.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:07.05,0:57:10.30,Default,,0,0,0,,VIOLET: They can't be real people.\NWONKA: Of course they are.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:10.39,0:57:11.64,Default,,0,0,0,,MR. SALT: Stuff and nonsense!
Dialogue: 0,0:57:11.72,0:57:13.43,Default,,0,0,0,,No, Oompa Loompas.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:14.77,0:57:17.90,Default,,0,0,0,,- From Loompaland.\N- Loompaland? There's no such place.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:17.98,0:57:20.94,Default,,0,0,0,,- Excuse me, dear lady-\N- I am a geography teacher.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:21.02,0:57:24.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Then you know all about it\Nand what a terrible country it is.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:24.49,0:57:27.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Nothing but desolate wastes\Nand fierce beasts.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:27.82,0:57:30.99,Default,,0,0,0,,The poor little Oompa Loompas\Nwere so small and helpless...
Dialogue: 0,0:57:31.08,0:57:33.00,Default,,0,0,0,,they would get gobbled up right and left.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:33.08,0:57:37.38,Default,,0,0,0,,A Wangdoodle would eat 10 of them\Nfor breakfast and think nothing of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:37.50,0:57:38.84,Default,,0,0,0,,And so I said:
Dialogue: 0,0:57:39.17,0:57:41.96,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}" Come and live with me\Nin peace and safety...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:57:42.17,0:57:45.17,Default,,0,0,0,," away from all the Wangdoodles\Nand Hornswogglers...
Dialogue: 0,0:57:45.26,0:57:48.76,Default,,0,0,0,," and Snozzwangers\Nand rotten Vermicious Knids. "
Dialogue: 0,0:57:48.84,0:57:52.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Snozzwangers? Vermicious Knids?\NWhat kind of rubbish is that?
Dialogue: 0,0:57:52.97,0:57:55.85,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry, but all questions\Nmust be submitted in writing.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:55.93,0:57:58.02,Default,,0,0,0,,So, in the greatest of secrecy...
Dialogue: 0,0:57:58.10,0:58:01.77,Default,,0,0,0,,I transported the entire population\Nof Oompa Loompas to my factory.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:01.86,0:58:05.86,Default,,0,0,0,,I want an Oompa Loompa.\NI want you to get me one right away.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:05.94,0:58:08.82,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, I'll get you one\Nbefore the day's out.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:08.95,0:58:11.29,Default,,0,0,0,,I want an Oompa Loompa now.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:11.37,0:58:12.87,Default,,0,0,0,,VIOLET: Can it, you nit!
Dialogue: 0,0:58:13.41,0:58:15.16,Default,,0,0,0,,AUGUSTUS: This stuff is terrific.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:15.66,0:58:18.87,Default,,0,0,0,,CHARLIE: Look at Augustus.\NGRANDPA: Don't worry, he can't drink it all.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:19.29,0:58:22.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Augustus, sweetheart,\Nsave some room for later.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:58:23.13,0:58:27.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Please don't do that. My chocolate\Nmust never be touched by human hands.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:27.67,0:58:30.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't do that!\NYou're contaminating my entire river.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:30.80,0:58:32.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Please, I beg you! Augustus!
Dialogue: 0,0:58:33.06,0:58:34.31,Default,,0,0,0,,[Exclaiming]
Dialogue: 0,0:58:34.39,0:58:36.31,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: My chocolate!\NAUGUSTUS: Help!
Dialogue: 0,0:58:37.98,0:58:40.36,Default,,0,0,0,,My chocolate. My beautiful chocolate.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:41.61,0:58:44.15,Default,,0,0,0,,MRS. GLOOP: Don't just stand there.\NDo something!
Dialogue: 0,0:58:44.23,0:58:46.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Help. Police. Murder.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:46.57,0:58:49.82,Default,,0,0,0,,GRANDPA: Quick, Charlie. Here.\NCHARLIE: Quick, Augustus, grab this.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:50.28,0:58:51.74,Default,,0,0,0,,MRS. TEEVEE: What's happening to him?
Dialogue: 0,0:58:51.82,0:58:54.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}MR. SALT: He's drowning.\NMRS. GLOOP: Dive in. Save him!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:58:54.24,0:58:55.32,Default,,0,0,0,,It's too late.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:55.41,0:58:58.04,Default,,0,0,0,,- Too late?\N- He's had it now. The suction's got him.
Dialogue: 0,0:58:58.12,0:58:59.91,Default,,0,0,0,,MRS. GLOOP: Augustus, come back!
Dialogue: 0,0:59:00.00,0:59:02.50,Default,,0,0,0,,- Where is he?\N- Watch the pipe.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:03.00,0:59:05.21,Default,,0,0,0,,VERUCA: How long is he going to\Nstay down, Daddy?
Dialogue: 0,0:59:05.30,0:59:08.26,Default,,0,0,0,,MRS. GLOOP: He can't swim.\NWONKA: There's no better time to learn.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:08.34,0:59:11.34,Default,,0,0,0,,MIKE: His coat's going up the pipe.\NSAM: Call a plumber.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:11.43,0:59:13.52,Default,,0,0,0,,MR. SALT: He's stuck in the pipe, isn't he?
Dialogue: 0,0:59:13.60,0:59:16.02,Default,,0,0,0,,- It's his stomach that's done that.\N- Help!
Dialogue: 0,0:59:16.10,0:59:19.02,Default,,0,0,0,,VIOLET: He's blocking the chocolate.\NGRANDPA: What happens now?
Dialogue: 0,0:59:19.10,0:59:23.35,Default,,0,0,0,,The pressure will get him out.\NIt's building up behind the blockage.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:23.98,0:59:26.69,Default,,0,0,0,,MR. SALT: How long is it going to take\Nto push through?
Dialogue: 0,0:59:26.78,0:59:30.24,Default,,0,0,0,,The suspense is terrible. I hope it'll last.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:30.32,0:59:31.61,Default,,0,0,0,,MR. SALT: Go on, boy.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:33.37,0:59:36.37,Default,,0,0,0,,CHARLIE: He'll never get out.\NGRANDPA: Yes, he will. Watch.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:36.45,0:59:39.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Remember you once asked me\Nhow a bullet comes out of a gun?
Dialogue: 0,0:59:40.75,0:59:43.30,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}He'll be made into marshmallows\Nin five seconds.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,0:59:43.38,0:59:46.72,Default,,0,0,0,,- Impossible. That's absurd, unthinkable.\N- Why?
Dialogue: 0,0:59:47.05,0:59:49.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Because that pipe goes\Nto the Fudge Room.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:49.63,0:59:51.30,Default,,0,0,0,,MRS. GLOOP: You terrible man.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:53.72,0:59:56.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Take Mrs. Gloop to the Fudge Room,\Nbut look sharp...
Dialogue: 0,0:59:56.56,0:59:58.77,Default,,0,0,0,,or her little boy will get poured into the boiler.
Dialogue: 0,0:59:58.85,1:00:00.60,Default,,0,0,0,,You boiled him up, I know it.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:00.68,1:00:04.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Nil desperandum, dear lady. Across\Nthe desert lies the Promised Land.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:00:04.73,1:00:06.23,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: Goodbye, Mrs. Gloop.
Dialogue: 0,1:00:06.32,1:00:10.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}WONKA: Adieu. Auf Wiedersehen.\NGesundheit. Farewell.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:00:11.57,1:00:14.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Singing] Oompa Loompa Doompadee Do{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:00:14.74,1:00:17.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I've got a perfect puzzle for you{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:00:18.08,1:00:21.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oompa Loompa Doompadee Dee{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:00:21.33,1:00:24.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If you are wise you'll listen to me{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:00:24.67,1:00:27.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What do you get\Nwhen you guzzle down sweets?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:00:28.00,1:00:31.00,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Eating as much as an elephant eats?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:00:31.26,1:00:34.26,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What are you at getting terribly fat?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:00:34.43,1:00:38.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What do you think will come of that?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:00:39.35,1:00:41.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I don't like the look of it{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:00:41.23,1:00:44.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oompa Loompa Doompadee Da{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:00:44.27,1:00:47.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If you're not greedy, you will go far{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:00:47.61,1:00:50.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You will live in happiness, too{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:00:50.94,1:00:54.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Like the Oompa Loompa Doompadee Do{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:01:04.46,1:01:07.63,Default,,0,0,0,,What kind of place\Nare you running here, anyhow, Wonka?
Dialogue: 0,1:01:07.79,1:01:09.21,Default,,0,0,0,,[Speaking in French]
Dialogue: 0,1:01:11.38,1:01:12.80,Default,,0,0,0,,What's he talking about?
Dialogue: 0,1:01:21.97,1:01:24.76,Default,,0,0,0,,[Soft instrumental music]
Dialogue: 0,1:01:31.82,1:01:33.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Wow, what a boat!
Dialogue: 0,1:01:33.32,1:01:35.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Looks good enough to eat.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:35.28,1:01:38.07,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}That's quite a nice little canoe\Nyou've got there, Wonka.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:01:38.16,1:01:42.21,Default,,0,0,0,," All I ask is a tall ship\Nand a star to sail her by"
Dialogue: 0,1:01:42.41,1:01:45.83,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: All aboard, everybody.\NMR. SALT: Ladies first. That means Veruca.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:45.91,1:01:48.83,Default,,0,0,0,,If she's a lady, I'm a Vermicious Knid.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:48.92,1:01:52.76,Default,,0,0,0,,- You sure this thing will float, eh. Wonka ?\N- With your buoyancy, sir. Rest assured.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:52.84,1:01:55.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}She's tr�s jolie, but is she seaworthy?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:01:55.09,1:01:58.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Nothing to worry about, my dear lady.\NI take good care of my guests.
Dialogue: 0,1:01:59.01,1:02:02.93,Default,,0,0,0,,- Yeah, you took real good care of that August kid\N..over there, yeah sure.\N- Everybody aboard.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:04.35,1:02:06.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You're going to love this.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:02:06.44,1:02:07.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Just love it.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:02:08.40,1:02:10.03,Default,,0,0,0,,[Bell ringing]
Dialogue: 0,1:02:13.73,1:02:15.90,Default,,0,0,0,,[Lilting instrumental music]
Dialogue: 0,1:02:38.30,1:02:42.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Daddy, I want a boat like this.\NA beautiful paddle boat, that's what i want.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:42.35,1:02:45.02,Default,,0,0,0,,What she wants\Nis a good kick in the pants.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:45.10,1:02:46.69,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm going to be seasick.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:46.77,1:02:48.48,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: Here, try one of this.\NMRS. TEEVEE: What are they?
Dialogue: 0,1:02:48.56,1:02:51.27,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: Rainbow drops.\NSuck 'em, you can spit in seven colors.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:51.36,1:02:52.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Spitting's a dirty habit.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:52.94,1:02:54.53,Default,,0,0,0,,I know a worse one.
Dialogue: 0,1:02:54.98,1:02:57.65,Default,,0,0,0,,[Lilting instrumental music continues]
Dialogue: 0,1:03:06.41,1:03:09.25,Default,,0,0,0,,- What business are you in, Salt?\N- Nuts.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:19.93,1:03:21.35,Default,,0,0,0,,[Tense instrumental music]
Dialogue: 0,1:03:21.43,1:03:22.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Here.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:22.68,1:03:26.35,Default,,0,0,0,,A small step for mankind,\Nbut a giant step for us.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:26.68,1:03:30.23,Default,,0,0,0,,- All ashore.\N- Let me off this freight.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:30.31,1:03:33.69,Default,,0,0,0,,MIKE: Why don't they show stuff like that\Non TV?
Dialogue: 0,1:03:33.77,1:03:37.48,Default,,0,0,0,,- What a nightmare.\N- Daddy, I do not want a boat like this.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:37.65,1:03:38.61,Default,,0,0,0,,CHARLIE: " Dairy Cream. "
Dialogue: 0,1:03:42.70,1:03:44.33,Default,,0,0,0,,BOTH: " Hair cream"?
Dialogue: 0,1:03:44.53,1:03:47.45,Default,,0,0,0,,[Wonka speaking in German]
Dialogue: 0,1:03:47.74,1:03:49.20,Default,,0,0,0,,That's not French.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:49.45,1:03:51.83,Default,,0,0,0,,[Continues speaking in German]
Dialogue: 0,1:03:55.71,1:03:57.67,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't take much more of this.
Dialogue: 0,1:03:59.71,1:04:01.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Der Inventing Room.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:04:02.93,1:04:05.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Now remember, no messing about.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:05.55,1:04:08.39,Default,,0,0,0,,No touching, no tasting, no telling.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:08.47,1:04:09.56,Default,,0,0,0,,GRANDPA: No telling what?
Dialogue: 0,1:04:09.64,1:04:13.85,Default,,0,0,0,,All of my most secret inventions\Nare cooking and simmering in here.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:13.94,1:04:17.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Old Slugworth would give his false teeth\Nto get inside for five minutes.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:04:17.94,1:04:20.48,Default,,0,0,0,,So don't touch a thing.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:28.03,1:04:29.91,Default,,0,0,0,,[Electronic beeping]
Dialogue: 0,1:04:46.34,1:04:49.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Inventing Room?\NLooks more like a Turkish bath to me.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:49.47,1:04:52.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Even if Slugworth did get in here,\Nhe couldn't find anything.
Dialogue: 0,1:04:52.56,1:04:55.73,Default,,0,0,0,,- You got a garbage strike going on?\N- Who does your cleaning up?
Dialogue: 0,1:04:55.81,1:04:59.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Shouldn't you wear rubber gloves?\NYou'll have the health inspectors after you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:04:59.82,1:05:03.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Invention, my dear friends,\Nis 93% perspiration...
Dialogue: 0,1:05:03.74,1:05:05.91,Default,,0,0,0,,6% electricity...
Dialogue: 0,1:05:05.99,1:05:07.91,Default,,0,0,0,,4% evaporation...
Dialogue: 0,1:05:07.99,1:05:10.41,Default,,0,0,0,,and 2% butterscotch ripple.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:10.49,1:05:12.70,Default,,0,0,0,,MRS. TEEVEE: That's 105%.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:12.91,1:05:14.16,Default,,0,0,0,,MR. SALT: Any good?
Dialogue: 0,1:05:15.54,1:05:16.71,Default,,0,0,0,,[Ln high-pitched voice] Yes.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:17.08,1:05:18.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Excuse me.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:20.92,1:05:24.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Time is a precious thing. Never waste it.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:26.18,1:05:29.93,Default,,0,0,0,,- He's absolutely bonkers.\N- That's not bad.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:32.43,1:05:35.89,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: " In spring time\NThe only pretty ring time
Dialogue: 0,1:05:35.98,1:05:39.11,Default,,0,0,0,," Birds sing, hey ding a ding, ding
Dialogue: 0,1:05:39.19,1:05:42.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}" Sweet lovers love the spring"{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:05:42.82,1:05:44.20,Default,,0,0,0,,[Explosion]
Dialogue: 0,1:05:46.15,1:05:48.36,Default,,0,0,0,,I told you not to, silly boy.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:48.45,1:05:49.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Your teeth!
Dialogue: 0,1:05:49.95,1:05:51.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Boy, that's great stuff.
Dialogue: 0,1:05:51.91,1:05:55.54,Default,,0,0,0,,That's exploding candy for your enemies.\NGreat idea, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,1:05:55.62,1:05:58.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Not ready yet, though. Still too weak.\NNeeds more gelignite.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:08.39,1:06:09.77,Default,,0,0,0,,What's that for?
Dialogue: 0,1:06:09.89,1:06:11.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Gives it a little kick.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:17.23,1:06:19.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Butterscotch? Buttergin?
Dialogue: 0,1:06:19.48,1:06:21.65,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Got something going on inside, have you?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:06:21.73,1:06:24.65,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: " Candy is dandy\Nbut liquor is quicker. "
Dialogue: 0,1:06:28.32,1:06:30.82,Default,,0,0,0,,MIKE: What's the matter?\NToo hot, Mr. Wonka?
Dialogue: 0,1:06:30.91,1:06:33.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Too cold. Far too cold.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:33.16,1:06:35.50,Default,,0,0,0,,MR. SALT: That's gourmet cooking for you.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:36.33,1:06:38.37,Default,,0,0,0,,No! Don't, please.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:38.71,1:06:41.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Forgive me,\Nbut no one must look under there.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:06:41.29,1:06:44.79,Default,,0,0,0,,This is the most secret machine\Nin my entire factory.
Dialogue: 0,1:06:45.01,1:06:48.93,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: This will sizzle old Slugworth.\NCHARLIE: What does it do?
Dialogue: 0,1:06:50.09,1:06:52.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Would you like to see?
Dialogue: 0,1:06:54.64,1:06:56.52,Default,,0,0,0,,[Buzzing]
Dialogue: 0,1:07:15.54,1:07:17.04,Default,,0,0,0,,CHARLIE: But what does it do?
Dialogue: 0,1:07:17.12,1:07:19.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Can't you see?\NIt makes Everlasting Gobstoppers.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:19.96,1:07:22.05,Default,,0,0,0,,VIOLET: Did you say\NEverlasting Gobstoppers?
Dialogue: 0,1:07:22.13,1:07:25.55,Default,,0,0,0,,For children with very little pocket money.\NYou can suck them forever.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:25.63,1:07:27.34,Default,,0,0,0,,I want an Everlasting Gobstopper.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:27.42,1:07:28.80,Default,,0,0,0,,- Me, too.\N- And me.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:28.88,1:07:31.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Fantastic invention.\NRevolutionize the industry.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:31.47,1:07:35.22,Default,,0,0,0,,You can suck them and suck them\Nand they'll never get any smaller. Never.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:35.31,1:07:36.56,Default,,0,0,0,,At least, I don't think so.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:36.64,1:07:38.81,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: Few more tests.\NMIKE: How do you make them?
Dialogue: 0,1:07:38.89,1:07:42.56,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm a trifle deaf in this ear.\NSpeak a little louder next time.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:42.65,1:07:44.32,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: Who wants\Nan Everlasting Gobstopper?
Dialogue: 0,1:07:44.40,1:07:46.07,Default,,0,0,0,,CHILDREN: I do.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:47.07,1:07:51.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I can only give them to you\Nif you swear to keep them for yourselves...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:07:51.66,1:07:56.04,Default,,0,0,0,,and never show them to another\Nliving soul as long as you all shall live.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:56.24,1:07:58.12,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: Agreed?\NCHILDREN: Agreed.
Dialogue: 0,1:07:58.33,1:08:01.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Good. One for you,\Nand one for you, and one for you.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:02.04,1:08:03.54,Default,,0,0,0,,What about Charlie?
Dialogue: 0,1:08:03.67,1:08:05.09,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: And one for Charlie.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:05.17,1:08:07.67,Default,,0,0,0,,She's got two. I want another one.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:07.75,1:08:10.67,Default,,0,0,0,,VIOLET: Stop squawking, you twit!\NWONKA: Everybody has had one.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:10.76,1:08:14.01,Default,,0,0,0,,And one is enough for anybody.\NNow come along.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:15.72,1:08:17.35,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: Over here, if you'll follow me...
Dialogue: 0,1:08:17.76,1:08:19.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I have something rather special\Nto show you.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:08:20.02,1:08:21.73,Default,,0,0,0,,MR. SALT: It's special, all right.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:22.02,1:08:24.36,Default,,0,0,0,,I only hope my Veruca doesn't want one.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:24.44,1:08:26.94,Default,,0,0,0,,MIKE: What a contraption.\NWONKA: Isn't she scrumptious?
Dialogue: 0,1:08:27.02,1:08:30.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}She's my revolutionary,\Nnon-pollutionary mechanical wonder.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:08:30.82,1:08:33.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Button, button, who's got the button?
Dialogue: 0,1:08:33.78,1:08:35.28,Default,,0,0,0,,CHARLIE: It's over there.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:35.87,1:08:37.04,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: Here?\NCHARLIE: Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:37.49,1:08:39.74,Default,,0,0,0,,[Whizzing and whirring]
Dialogue: 0,1:08:53.13,1:08:55.38,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: What you are witnessing,\Ndear friends...
Dialogue: 0,1:08:55.47,1:08:58.26,Default,,0,0,0,,is the most enormous miracle\Nof the Machine Age.
Dialogue: 0,1:08:58.35,1:09:01.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The creation of a confectionery giant.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:09:02.60,1:09:05.19,Default,,0,0,0,,[Whizzing and whirring continues]
Dialogue: 0,1:09:11.23,1:09:13.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}WONKA: Finito.\NVERUCA: That's all?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:09:13.49,1:09:15.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't you know what this is?
Dialogue: 0,1:09:15.57,1:09:17.45,Default,,0,0,0,,VIOLET: By gum, it's gum!\NWONKA: Wrong.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:17.53,1:09:21.37,Default,,0,0,0,,It's the most amazing, fabulous,\Nsensational gum in the whole world.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:21.45,1:09:22.74,Default,,0,0,0,,What's so fab about it?
Dialogue: 0,1:09:22.83,1:09:26.08,Default,,0,0,0,,- This tiny gum is a three-course dinner.\N- Bull.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:26.17,1:09:29.34,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: Roast beef, it's not quite right yet.\NVIOLET: I don't care.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:29.42,1:09:31.51,Default,,0,0,0,,I wouldn't do that. I really wouldn't.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:31.59,1:09:33.43,Default,,0,0,0,,So long as it's gum, that's for me.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:33.51,1:09:35.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Violet, don't do anything stupid.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:35.84,1:09:37.84,Default,,0,0,0,,What's it taste like?
Dialogue: 0,1:09:37.93,1:09:40.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Madness! It's tomato soup.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:40.93,1:09:44.02,Default,,0,0,0,,It's hot and creamy.\NI can feel it running down my throat.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:44.10,1:09:45.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Stop. Don't.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:45.64,1:09:49.81,Default,,0,0,0,,- Why doesn't she listen to Mr. Wonka?\N- Because, Charlie, she's a nitwit.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:49.90,1:09:51.65,Default,,0,0,0,,This sure is great soup.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:51.78,1:09:53.70,Default,,0,0,0,,The second course is coming up.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:53.78,1:09:56.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Roast beef and a baked potato.
Dialogue: 0,1:09:56.66,1:09:58.41,Default,,0,0,0,,With sour cream?
Dialogue: 0,1:09:59.62,1:10:02.79,Default,,0,0,0,,SAM: What's for dessert, baby?\NVIOLET: Dessert? Here it comes.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:02.87,1:10:06.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Blueberry pie and cream.\NIt's the most marvelous pie I've tasted.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:10:06.96,1:10:09.25,Default,,0,0,0,,SAM: Holy Toledo!\NWhat's happening to your face?
Dialogue: 0,1:10:09.33,1:10:10.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Cool it, Dad. Let me finish.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:11.04,1:10:12.79,Default,,0,0,0,,But your face is turning blue.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:12.88,1:10:16.26,Default,,0,0,0,,SAM: You're turning violet, Violet!\NVIOLET: What are you talking about?
Dialogue: 0,1:10:16.34,1:10:18.43,Default,,0,0,0,,I told you I hadn't got it right yet.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:18.51,1:10:21.14,Default,,0,0,0,,You can say that again.\NLook what it's done to my kid.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:21.22,1:10:24.97,Default,,0,0,0,,It always goes wrong\Nwhen we come to the dessert. Always.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:25.10,1:10:27.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Violet, what are you doing now?
Dialogue: 0,1:10:27.14,1:10:29.06,Default,,0,0,0,,- You're blowing up!\N- I feel funny!
Dialogue: 0,1:10:29.15,1:10:31.40,Default,,0,0,0,,GRANDPA: I'm not surprised.\NVIOLET: What's happening?
Dialogue: 0,1:10:31.48,1:10:33.48,Default,,0,0,0,,SAM: You're blowing up!\NWONKA: Like a blueberry.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:33.57,1:10:35.91,Default,,0,0,0,,SAM: Call a doctor!\NMRS. TEEVEE: Stick her with a pin.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:35.99,1:10:38.49,Default,,0,0,0,,CHARLIE: She'll pop.\NWONKA: It happens every time.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:38.57,1:10:41.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}- They all become blueberries.\N- You've really done it this time!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:10:41.83,1:10:43.50,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll break you for this.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:43.58,1:10:46.79,Default,,0,0,0,,- Well, I'll get it right in the end.\N- Help!
Dialogue: 0,1:10:47.58,1:10:50.75,Default,,0,0,0,,SAM: Let the air out of her quick.\NWONKA: There's no air.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:50.83,1:10:52.58,Default,,0,0,0,,- That's juice.\N- Juice?
Dialogue: 0,1:10:52.67,1:10:55.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Would you roll the young lady\Ndown to the juicing room at once?
Dialogue: 0,1:10:55.96,1:10:58.00,Default,,0,0,0,,SAM: What for?\NWONKA: For squeezing.
Dialogue: 0,1:10:58.09,1:11:00.68,Default,,0,0,0,,She has to be squeezed immediately\Nbefore she explodes.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:00.76,1:11:03.35,Default,,0,0,0,,- Explodes?\N- It's a fairly simple operation.
Dialogue: 0,1:11:03.43,1:11:07.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Singing] Oompa Loompa Doompadee Do{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:11:07.27,1:11:10.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I've got another puzzle for you{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:11:10.94,1:11:14.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oompa Loompa Doompada Dee{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:11:14.69,1:11:18.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If you are wise you'll listen to me{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:11:18.40,1:11:21.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Gum chewing's fine\NWhen it's once in a while{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:11:21.70,1:11:25.54,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It stops you from smoking\NAnd brightens your smile{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:11:25.62,1:11:28.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But it's repulsive, revolting, and wrong{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:11:29.04,1:11:33.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Chewing and chewing all day long{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:11:34.71,1:11:36.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The way that a cow does{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:11:38.30,1:11:41.89,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oompa Loompa Doompadee Da{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:11:41.97,1:11:45.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Given good manners, you will go far{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:11:45.64,1:11:48.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You will live in happiness, too{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:11:49.14,1:11:53.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Like the Oompa Loompa Doompadee Do{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:11:57.65,1:12:01.07,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll get even with you for this,\Nif it's the last thing I ever do!
Dialogue: 0,1:12:01.15,1:12:03.74,Default,,0,0,0,,I got a blueberry for a daughter.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:04.70,1:12:08.50,Default,,0,0,0,," Where is fancy bred,\NIn the heart or in the head?"
Dialogue: 0,1:12:09.96,1:12:11.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Shall we roll on?
Dialogue: 0,1:12:16.04,1:12:17.38,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:17.92,1:12:22.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, well, two naughty,\Nnasty little children gone.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:22.93,1:12:26.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Three good, sweet little children left.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:28.43,1:12:31.18,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: Hurry, please. Long way to go yet.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:34.77,1:12:36.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait a minute. I must show you this.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:37.11,1:12:39.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Lickable wallpaper for nursery walls.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:39.94,1:12:41.82,Default,,0,0,0,,Lick an orange, it tastes like an orange.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:41.90,1:12:45.74,Default,,0,0,0,,Lick a pineapple, it tastes like a pineapple.\NGo ahead, try it.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:46.16,1:12:48.04,Default,,0,0,0,,MRS. TEEVEE: I got a plum.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:48.12,1:12:51.79,Default,,0,0,0,,CHARLIE: Grandpa, this banana's fantastic.\NIt tastes so real.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:52.00,1:12:55.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Try some more.\NThe strawberries taste like strawberries.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:55.29,1:12:57.79,Default,,0,0,0,,The snozzberries taste like snozzberries.
Dialogue: 0,1:12:57.88,1:13:00.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Snozzberries?\NWhoever heard of a snozzberry?
Dialogue: 0,1:13:02.09,1:13:04.51,Default,,0,0,0,," We are the music makers.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:04.84,1:13:07.80,Default,,0,0,0,," And we are the dreamers of dreams. "
Dialogue: 0,1:13:09.26,1:13:10.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Come along.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:13.77,1:13:16.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Something very unusual in here.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:16.86,1:13:20.16,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: Bubbles, bubbles everywhere,\Nbut not a drop to drink.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:20.23,1:13:23.03,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: Yet.\NCHARLIE: What's it making, Mr. Wonka?
Dialogue: 0,1:13:23.11,1:13:25.53,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: Fizzy-Lifting drinks.\NThey fill you with gas...
Dialogue: 0,1:13:25.61,1:13:29.74,Default,,0,0,0,,and the gas is so lifting, that it lifts you\Nright off the ground like a balloon.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:29.83,1:13:32.17,Default,,0,0,0,,VERUCA: Isn't it high? Gosh!
Dialogue: 0,1:13:32.33,1:13:36.38,Default,,0,0,0,,- But I dare not sell it yet. It's too powerful.\N- Let us try some, please.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:36.46,1:13:40.84,Default,,0,0,0,,No, absolutely not. There'd be children\Nfloating around all over the place.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:41.05,1:13:43.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Come along, don't hang about.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:43.63,1:13:46.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You'll be wild about this next room.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:13:47.14,1:13:49.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's take a drink. Nobody's watching.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:49.89,1:13:51.64,Default,,0,0,0,,A small one won't hurt us.
Dialogue: 0,1:13:57.65,1:13:58.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Not bad.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:00.65,1:14:01.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Well?
Dialogue: 0,1:14:02.15,1:14:03.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Nothing's happening.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:03.99,1:14:06.70,Default,,0,0,0,,GRANDPA: You're right, Charlie.\NI can't understand why.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:06.78,1:14:08.16,Default,,0,0,0,,[Grandpa shrieks]
Dialogue: 0,1:14:09.66,1:14:11.37,Default,,0,0,0,,I feel terribly strange.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:11.49,1:14:14.33,Default,,0,0,0,,- What do we do now?\N- I don't know, Charlie.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:14.75,1:14:17.55,Default,,0,0,0,,We're in big trouble.\NMr. Wonka isn't going to like this.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:17.62,1:14:19.33,Default,,0,0,0,,We can't stay up here all day.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:19.42,1:14:21.46,Default,,0,0,0,,- You're right but-\N- I'll try and get down.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:21.55,1:14:24.55,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, Charlie,\Nbut please be very careful.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:25.76,1:14:29.51,Default,,0,0,0,,It's fun, Grandpa. It works.\NCome on in, the air's fine.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:29.59,1:14:32.68,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}- I haven't been swimming in 20 years.\N- Give me your hand.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:14:32.76,1:14:34.68,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't think I ought to.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:34.81,1:14:37.10,Default,,0,0,0,,[Light instrumental music]
Dialogue: 0,1:14:37.35,1:14:39.27,Default,,0,0,0,,This is great!
Dialogue: 0,1:14:39.69,1:14:43.15,Default,,0,0,0,,CHARLIE: Try this, Grandpa.\NGRANDPA: All right, Charlie. Wait for me.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:43.61,1:14:47.07,Default,,0,0,0,,[Grandpa and Charlie squeal with delight]
Dialogue: 0,1:14:47.53,1:14:50.41,Default,,0,0,0,,GRANDPA: I'm a shooting star.\NCHARLIE: I'm a rocket!
Dialogue: 0,1:14:51.87,1:14:53.75,Default,,0,0,0,,This is really great.
Dialogue: 0,1:14:53.87,1:14:56.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Look, I'm a bird!
Dialogue: 0,1:14:58.04,1:15:00.21,Default,,0,0,0,,GRANDPA: I feel light as a feather.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:01.04,1:15:03.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Look down. We're really high now.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:08.47,1:15:10.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Watch this, Grandpa.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:13.72,1:15:15.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Wonderful, Charlie.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:15.39,1:15:17.73,Default,,0,0,0,,- Try it, Grandpa.\N- I don't know.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:17.81,1:15:20.44,Default,,0,0,0,,- Come on, Grandpa.\N- All right.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:23.32,1:15:25.28,Default,,0,0,0,,You did it, Grandpa!
Dialogue: 0,1:15:25.73,1:15:26.81,Default,,0,0,0,,[Grandpa groans]
Dialogue: 0,1:15:26.90,1:15:28.82,Default,,0,0,0,,I think I hit an air pocket.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:28.90,1:15:31.07,Default,,0,0,0,,You can fly to the moon this way.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:31.16,1:15:32.91,Default,,0,0,0,,GRANDPA: Let's just fly south\Nfor the winter.
Dialogue: 0,1:15:32.99,1:15:34.28,Default,,0,0,0,,CHARLIE: Why not?
Dialogue: 0,1:15:36.50,1:15:39.25,Default,,0,0,0,,- I'm a bird!\N- I'm a plane!
Dialogue: 0,1:15:39.33,1:15:40.58,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm...
Dialogue: 0,1:15:40.67,1:15:42.51,Default,,0,0,0,,going too high!
Dialogue: 0,1:15:43.34,1:15:45.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Grandpa, I can't get down!
Dialogue: 0,1:15:45.71,1:15:48.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Help! Grandpa, the fan!
Dialogue: 0,1:15:48.67,1:15:51.01,Default,,0,0,0,,GRANDPA: Stay away from it!\NIt'll chop us to bits!
Dialogue: 0,1:15:51.09,1:15:55.01,Default,,0,0,0,,GRANDPA: We're in trouble! I can't stop!\NCHARLIE: It's pulling me in!
Dialogue: 0,1:15:55.10,1:15:56.98,Default,,0,0,0,,GRANDPA: I can't stop!
Dialogue: 0,1:15:57.18,1:16:00.10,Default,,0,0,0,,CHARLIE: What do we do?\NGRANDPA: Grab hold of something quick!
Dialogue: 0,1:16:00.19,1:16:02.78,Default,,0,0,0,,CHARLIE: There's nothing\Nto grab on to! Help!
Dialogue: 0,1:16:03.06,1:16:06.52,Default,,0,0,0,,CHARLIE: We're gonna get killed!\NGRANDPA: Help!
Dialogue: 0,1:16:06.61,1:16:09.45,Default,,0,0,0,,Mr. Wonka, please! Turn off the fan!
Dialogue: 0,1:16:10.40,1:16:11.44,Default,,0,0,0,,[Burping]
Dialogue: 0,1:16:12.99,1:16:15.87,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm going down. Quick, Charlie, burp!
Dialogue: 0,1:16:15.95,1:16:18.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If you don't, it'll cut you to ribbons!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:16:18.29,1:16:20.00,Default,,0,0,0,,CHARLIE: I can't! Help!
Dialogue: 0,1:16:20.08,1:16:21.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You've got to burp. It's the only way.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:16:22.62,1:16:24.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Attaboy. Burp again.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:16:25.13,1:16:27.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Attaboy. Come on.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:16:28.05,1:16:29.09,Default,,0,0,0,,[Charlie burping]
Dialogue: 0,1:16:29.30,1:16:31.47,Default,,0,0,0,,That's wonderful, Charlie.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:37.97,1:16:41.27,Default,,0,0,0,,GRANDPA: Grab on to me.\NWe're going to be all right now.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:41.52,1:16:43.40,Default,,0,0,0,,[Both burping]
Dialogue: 0,1:16:45.40,1:16:48.11,Default,,0,0,0,,[Light instrumental music]
Dialogue: 0,1:16:49.19,1:16:50.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Good boy.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:50.99,1:16:53.45,Default,,0,0,0,,From now on,\Nwe keep our feet on the ground.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:53.53,1:16:55.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's catch up to the others.
Dialogue: 0,1:16:58.33,1:17:02.17,Default,,0,0,0,,I know what you're thinking.\NThey can't be doing what they're doing.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:02.37,1:17:04.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But they are. They have to.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:17:04.46,1:17:07.25,Default,,0,0,0,,I haven't met the Oompa Loompa yet\Nwho could do it.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:07.34,1:17:09.68,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: These are the geese\Nthat lay the golden eggs.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:09.76,1:17:11.89,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: They're larger\Nthan ordinary geese.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:11.97,1:17:16.10,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: In fact, they're quadruple-size\Ngeese which produce octuple-size eggs.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:16.18,1:17:18.18,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: They're laying overtime for Easter.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:18.26,1:17:20.01,Default,,0,0,0,,But Easter's over.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:20.43,1:17:24.35,Default,,0,0,0,,[Whispering] They don't know that.\NI'm trying to get ahead for next year.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:25.69,1:17:28.28,Default,,0,0,0,,MR. SALT: What happens\Nif they drop one of those eggs?
Dialogue: 0,1:17:28.36,1:17:30.95,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: An omelet fit for a king, sir.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:31.28,1:17:32.99,Default,,0,0,0,,VERUCA: Are they chocolate eggs?
Dialogue: 0,1:17:33.11,1:17:35.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Golden chocolate eggs.\NThat's a great delicacy.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:36.11,1:17:37.70,Default,,0,0,0,,But don't get too close.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:37.78,1:17:40.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The geese are temperamental.\NSo we have the Eggdicator.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:17:40.62,1:17:42.71,Default,,0,0,0,,MRS. TEEVEE: Egg-di-what?\NWONKA: The Eggdicator.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:42.79,1:17:45.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It can tell the difference\Nbetween a good egg...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:17:45.42,1:17:46.67,Default,,0,0,0,,and a bad egg.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:46.75,1:17:50.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If it's a good egg, it's shined up\Nand shipped out all over the world.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:17:50.71,1:17:52.63,Default,,0,0,0,,But if it's a bad egg...
Dialogue: 0,1:17:53.55,1:17:55.05,Default,,0,0,0,,down the chute.
Dialogue: 0,1:17:56.72,1:17:58.10,Default,,0,0,0,,[Horn honking]
Dialogue: 0,1:17:59.30,1:18:02.76,Default,,0,0,0,,- It's an educated Eggdicator.\N- It's a lot of nonsense.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:03.31,1:18:06.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Singing] A little nonsense now and then{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:18:06.48,1:18:09.82,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Is relished by the wisest men{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:18:10.32,1:18:12.24,Default,,0,0,0,,VERUCA: Daddy, I want a golden goose.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:12.48,1:18:15.44,Default,,0,0,0,,CHARLIE: Here we go again.\NMR. SALT: All right, sweetheart.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:15.65,1:18:17.99,Default,,0,0,0,,You'll get one as soon as we get home.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:18.07,1:18:20.41,Default,,0,0,0,,No, I want one of those.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:21.08,1:18:23.08,Default,,0,0,0,,How much do you want for the goose?
Dialogue: 0,1:18:23.16,1:18:25.50,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: They're not for sale.\NMR. SALT: Name your price.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:25.58,1:18:27.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}WONKA: She can't have one.\NVERUCA: Who says so?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:18:27.83,1:18:31.50,Default,,0,0,0,,- The man with the funny hat.\N- I want one. I want a golden goose.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:32.00,1:18:34.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Gooses. Geeses.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:34.67,1:18:37.42,Default,,0,0,0,,I want my geese\Nto lay golden eggs for Easter.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:37.51,1:18:39.85,Default,,0,0,0,,MR. SALT: It will, dear.\NVERUCA: At least 100 a day.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:39.93,1:18:42.93,Default,,0,0,0,,MR. SALT: Anything you say.\NVERUCA: And by the way...
Dialogue: 0,1:18:43.10,1:18:46.44,Default,,0,0,0,,VERUCA: I want a feast.\NMR. SALT: You ate before you came here.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:46.52,1:18:48.27,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Singing] I want a bean-feast{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:18:48.35,1:18:49.44,Default,,0,0,0,,One of those.
Dialogue: 0,1:18:49.52,1:18:52.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Singing] Cream buns and doughnuts\NAnd fruitcake with no nuts{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:18:52.61,1:18:54.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}So good you could go nuts{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:18:54.44,1:18:58.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}- You'll have them when you get home.\N- No, now. I want a ball.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:18:59.53,1:19:01.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Singing] I want a party{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:19:01.87,1:19:04.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Pink macaroons and a million balloons{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:19:04.24,1:19:06.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And performing baboons and...{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:19:06.54,1:19:07.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Give it to me{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:19:08.25,1:19:09.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Now.
Dialogue: 0,1:19:09.46,1:19:11.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Singing] I want the world{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:19:11.79,1:19:14.13,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I want the whole world{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:19:14.30,1:19:18.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I want to lock it all up in my pocket\NIt's my bar of chocolate{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:19:18.80,1:19:21.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Give it to me now{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:19:21.97,1:19:23.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I want today{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:19:24.31,1:19:26.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I want tomorrow{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:19:26.56,1:19:29.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I want to wear them\NLike braids in my hair{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:19:29.39,1:19:31.48,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And I don't want to share them!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:19:35.32,1:19:38.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I want a party with roomfuls of laughter{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:19:39.15,1:19:41.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Ten thousand tons of ice cream{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:19:42.16,1:19:45.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And if I don't get the things I am after{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:19:46.75,1:19:50.71,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'm going to scream{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:20:00.59,1:20:02.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I want the works{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:20:02.09,1:20:03.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I want the whole works{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:20:03.68,1:20:06.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Presents and prizes\NAnd sweets and surprises{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:20:06.52,1:20:09.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Of all shapes and sizes\NAnd now{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:20:09.43,1:20:13.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Don't care how\NI want it now{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:20:18.15,1:20:19.49,Default,,0,0,0,,[Horn honking]
Dialogue: 0,1:20:26.03,1:20:27.78,Default,,0,0,0,,She was a bad egg.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:29.16,1:20:30.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Where's she gone?
Dialogue: 0,1:20:30.71,1:20:33.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Where all the other bad eggs go.\NDown the garbage chute.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:34.13,1:20:36.13,Default,,0,0,0,,The garbage chute?
Dialogue: 0,1:20:36.71,1:20:39.51,Default,,0,0,0,,- Where does it lead to?\N- To the furnace.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:40.22,1:20:42.06,Default,,0,0,0,,The furnace?
Dialogue: 0,1:20:42.72,1:20:45.81,Default,,0,0,0,,- She'll be sizzled like a sausage.\N- Not necessarily.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:45.89,1:20:48.35,Default,,0,0,0,,She could be stuck inside the tube.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:48.60,1:20:49.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Hold on!
Dialogue: 0,1:20:49.81,1:20:52.90,Default,,0,0,0,,MR. SALT: Veruca, sweetheart.\NDaddy's coming!
Dialogue: 0,1:20:55.98,1:20:58.15,Default,,0,0,0,,There's gonna be a lot of garbage today.
Dialogue: 0,1:20:58.23,1:21:01.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Mr. Salt finally got what he wanted.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:01.32,1:21:03.91,Default,,0,0,0,,- What's that?\N- Veruca went first.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:04.07,1:21:07.95,Default,,0,0,0,,CHARLIE: Mr. Wonka, they won't really\Nbe burned in the furnace, will they?
Dialogue: 0,1:21:08.83,1:21:11.75,Default,,0,0,0,,I think that furnace is lit\Nonly every other day.
Dialogue: 0,1:21:11.91,1:21:14.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}So they have a good sporting chance.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:21:15.25,1:21:18.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Singing] Oompa Loompa Doompadee Do{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:21:18.92,1:21:22.42,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I've got another puzzle for you{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:21:22.59,1:21:25.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oompa Loompa Doompadee Dee{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:21:26.18,1:21:29.60,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If you are wise you'll listen to me{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:21:29.85,1:21:33.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Who do you blame when your kid is a brat{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:21:33.39,1:21:36.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Pampered and spoiled like a Siamese cat?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:21:36.86,1:21:40.20,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Blaming the kids is a lie and a shame{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:21:40.28,1:21:44.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You know exactly who's to blame{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:21:45.11,1:21:47.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The mother and the father{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:21:48.95,1:21:52.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oompa Loompa Doompadee Da{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:21:52.45,1:21:55.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If you're not spoiled then you will go far{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:21:56.12,1:22:00.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You will live in happiness, too{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:22:01.38,1:22:05.55,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Like the Oompa Loompa Doompadee Do{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:22:06.76,1:22:09.72,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: I can't understand.\NThe children are disappearing like rabbits.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:09.81,1:22:13.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Well, we still have each other.\NShall we press on?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:22:13.14,1:22:15.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Can't we sit down for a minute?
Dialogue: 0,1:22:15.31,1:22:19.48,Default,,0,0,0,,- The pace is killing me.\N- Transportation has been arranged.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:24.15,1:22:26.24,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: Behold the Wonkamobile.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:26.32,1:22:28.57,Default,,0,0,0,," A thing of beauty is a joy forever. "
Dialogue: 0,1:22:28.66,1:22:31.50,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: Places, please.\NThe dance is about to begin.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:31.62,1:22:34.25,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: Better grab a seat,\Nthey're going fast.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:34.50,1:22:37.00,Default,,0,0,0,,GRANDPA: What's that\Nthey're filling it up with?
Dialogue: 0,1:22:37.17,1:22:40.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Ginger ale, ginger pop,\Nginger beer, beer bubbles...
Dialogue: 0,1:22:40.17,1:22:43.59,Default,,0,0,0,,bubbleade, bubble cola, double cola,\Ndouble-bubble burp-a-cola...
Dialogue: 0,1:22:43.67,1:22:46.67,Default,,0,0,0,,and all that crazy carbonated stuff\Nthat tickles your nose.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:46.84,1:22:49.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Few people realize\Nthe tremendous power in those things.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:50.01,1:22:51.89,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry I asked.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:51.97,1:22:55.27,Default,,0,0,0,,[Whispering] You think Slugworth would\Npay extra to know about this?
Dialogue: 0,1:22:55.35,1:22:58.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Just keep your eyes open\Nand your mouth shut.
Dialogue: 0,1:22:59.81,1:23:02.60,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: Everybody set?\NCHARLIE: Is this gonna go fast?
Dialogue: 0,1:23:02.69,1:23:05.44,Default,,0,0,0,,It should. It's got more gas in it\Nthan a politician.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:05.53,1:23:09.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Hold on tight. I'm going to open her up\Nand see what she can do.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:17.71,1:23:19.71,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: " Swifter than eagles...
Dialogue: 0,1:23:20.00,1:23:22.04,Default,,0,0,0,," stronger than lions! "
Dialogue: 0,1:23:22.42,1:23:23.92,Default,,0,0,0,,[Screaming]
Dialogue: 0,1:23:30.01,1:23:31.72,Default,,0,0,0,,MIKE: It's getting in my eyes!
Dialogue: 0,1:23:32.35,1:23:34.23,Default,,0,0,0,,MRS. TEEVEE: It's seeping in my shoes!
Dialogue: 0,1:23:34.39,1:23:37.06,Default,,0,0,0,,MRS. TEEVEE: I'm soaked!\NIt'll never come out!
Dialogue: 0,1:23:37.35,1:23:39.06,Default,,0,0,0,,MIKE: It's sticking to my gun.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:40.90,1:23:42.49,Default,,0,0,0,,[Wonka singing]
Dialogue: 0,1:23:47.40,1:23:50.61,Default,,0,0,0,,My dress! My hair! My face!
Dialogue: 0,1:23:51.91,1:23:54.75,Default,,0,0,0,,MRS. TEEVEE: I'm sending you\Nthe cleaning bill, Mr. Wonka.
Dialogue: 0,1:23:57.87,1:23:59.75,Default,,0,0,0,,MRS. TEEVEE: I'm dry cleaned.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:05.05,1:24:06.64,Default,,0,0,0,,Grandpa, what was that\Nwe just went through?
Dialogue: 0,1:24:07.51,1:24:08.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Hsaw Aknow.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:08.88,1:24:09.96,Default,,0,0,0,,MRS. TEEVEE: Is that Japanese?
Dialogue: 0,1:24:10.05,1:24:12.18,Default,,0,0,0,,No, " Wonka Wash" spelled backwards.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:12.26,1:24:14.51,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: That's it. The journey's over.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:14.60,1:24:18.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}GRANDPA: Finest bath I've had in 20 years.\NCHARLIE: Let's do it again, Mr. Wonka.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:24:18.68,1:24:22.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}- That's as far as it goes?\N- Couldn't we have walked?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:24:22.52,1:24:26.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If the good Lord had intended us to walk,\Nhe wouldn't have invented roller skates.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:24:26.94,1:24:31.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Would you all please put these on?\NWe have to be very careful.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:24:31.70,1:24:34.04,Default,,0,0,0,,There's dangerous stuff inside.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:36.66,1:24:40.29,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: Wonkavision. My very latest\Nand greatest invention.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:41.21,1:24:43.55,Default,,0,0,0,,MIKE: It's television.\NWONKA: It's Wonkavision.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:43.63,1:24:46.80,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I suppose you all know\Nhow ordinary television works.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:24:46.88,1:24:49.47,Default,,0,0,0,,- You photograph-\N- I do. You photograph something...
Dialogue: 0,1:24:49.55,1:24:52.18,Default,,0,0,0,,then it's split into millions of pieces...
Dialogue: 0,1:24:52.26,1:24:56.81,Default,,0,0,0,,that go whizzing through the air\Nand down to your TV set in the right order.
Dialogue: 0,1:24:57.14,1:25:00.39,Default,,0,0,0,,You should open your mouth a little wider\Nwhen you speak.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:00.48,1:25:03.02,Default,,0,0,0,,So I thought,\N" If they can do it with a photograph...
Dialogue: 0,1:25:03.10,1:25:05.94,Default,,0,0,0,," why can't I do it with a bar of chocolate?"
Dialogue: 0,1:25:08.32,1:25:12.62,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: I shall now send this chocolate\Nbar from one end of the room to the other.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:12.70,1:25:16.33,Default,,0,0,0,,It has to be big, because when\Nyou transmit something by television...
Dialogue: 0,1:25:16.41,1:25:18.91,Default,,0,0,0,,it always ends up smaller\Non the other end.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:18.99,1:25:20.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Goggles on, please.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:22.71,1:25:25.96,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: Lights, camera, action!
Dialogue: 0,1:25:26.59,1:25:27.84,Default,,0,0,0,,[Screaming]
Dialogue: 0,1:25:28.09,1:25:30.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You can remove your goggles.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:25:30.34,1:25:32.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Where's the chocolate?
Dialogue: 0,1:25:32.09,1:25:34.84,Default,,0,0,0,,It's flying over our heads\Nin a million pieces.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:34.97,1:25:36.56,Default,,0,0,0,,[Electronic beeping]
Dialogue: 0,1:25:37.05,1:25:38.72,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: Now watch the screen.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:41.68,1:25:43.02,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: Here it comes.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:44.27,1:25:45.73,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: There it is.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:45.90,1:25:48.99,Default,,0,0,0,,- Take it.\N- How can you take it? It's just a picture.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:49.07,1:25:50.78,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, you take it.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:51.94,1:25:55.65,Default,,0,0,0,,- It's real.\N- Taste it. It's delicious. It's just smaller.
Dialogue: 0,1:25:58.37,1:26:00.62,Default,,0,0,0,,- It's perfect.\N- It's unbelievable.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:00.70,1:26:02.49,Default,,0,0,0,,- It's a miracle.\N- It's a TV dinner.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:02.58,1:26:05.29,Default,,0,0,0,,- It's Wonkavision.\N- It could change the world.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:05.37,1:26:07.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Can you send other things?
Dialogue: 0,1:26:07.21,1:26:09.55,Default,,0,0,0,,MIKE: Not just chocolate.\NWONKA: Anything you like.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:09.63,1:26:12.05,Default,,0,0,0,,- What about people?\N- People?
Dialogue: 0,1:26:14.05,1:26:16.76,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't really know. I suppose I could.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:16.97,1:26:19.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, I'm sure I could.\NI'm pretty sure I could.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:20.06,1:26:21.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}But it might have some messy results.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:26:22.06,1:26:25.40,Default,,0,0,0,,MIKE: Look! I'm going to be\Nthe first person to be sent by television.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:25.48,1:26:28.32,Default,,0,0,0,,MRS. TEEVEE: Get away from that thing!\NWONKA: Come back.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:28.40,1:26:30.49,Default,,0,0,0,,MIKE: Lights, camera, action!
Dialogue: 0,1:26:32.28,1:26:33.78,Default,,0,0,0,,[Electronic beeping]
Dialogue: 0,1:26:34.15,1:26:35.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Where are you?
Dialogue: 0,1:26:35.74,1:26:37.87,Default,,0,0,0,,GRANDPA: He's up there,\Nin a million pieces.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:37.95,1:26:39.87,Default,,0,0,0,,MRS. TEEVEE: Mike, are you there?
Dialogue: 0,1:26:39.95,1:26:41.87,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: No good shouting.\NWatch the screen.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:41.95,1:26:43.87,Default,,0,0,0,,[Electronic beeping continues]
Dialogue: 0,1:26:44.83,1:26:47.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Mike? Why is he taking so long?
Dialogue: 0,1:26:47.25,1:26:49.59,Default,,0,0,0,,A million pieces take a long time\Nto put together.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:49.67,1:26:52.51,Default,,0,0,0,,MRS. TEEVEE: Where are they?\NWONKA: There's something coming.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:52.59,1:26:55.34,Default,,0,0,0,,MRS. TEEVEE: Is it Mike?\NWONKA: It's hard to tell but-
Dialogue: 0,1:26:55.84,1:26:58.43,Default,,0,0,0,,The little groover's getting smaller\Nby the minute.
Dialogue: 0,1:26:58.51,1:27:02.72,Default,,0,0,0,,MIKE: Look at me. I'm the first person\Nin the world to be sent by television.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:03.47,1:27:05.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Wow, what a wild trip that was.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:06.10,1:27:08.77,Default,,0,0,0,,It's the greatest thing\Nthat's ever happened to me.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:08.85,1:27:12.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Am I coming in clear?\NMom, I said, am I coming in clear?
Dialogue: 0,1:27:12.61,1:27:14.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Great. He's completely unharmed.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:14.78,1:27:16.87,Default,,0,0,0,,You call that unharmed?
Dialogue: 0,1:27:16.95,1:27:20.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Wow, that was something.\NCan I do it again?
Dialogue: 0,1:27:20.28,1:27:22.03,Default,,0,0,0,,MRS. TEEVEE: No, there'll be nothing left.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:22.12,1:27:24.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't worry about a thing, Mom.\NI feel fine.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:24.45,1:27:26.37,Default,,0,0,0,,MIKE: I'm famous. I'm a TV star.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:26.46,1:27:28.80,Default,,0,0,0,,MIKE: Wait till the kids back home\Nhear about this.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:28.87,1:27:30.54,Default,,0,0,0,,MRS. TEEVEE: Nobody will.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:30.63,1:27:33.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Where are you taking me?\NI don't want to go in there.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:33.71,1:27:36.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Be quiet. Well?
Dialogue: 0,1:27:37.05,1:27:40.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Fortunately, small boys\Nare extremely springy and elastic.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:40.89,1:27:43.85,Default,,0,0,0,,So I think we'll put him\Nin my special taffy-pulling machine.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:43.93,1:27:44.97,Default,,0,0,0,,That should do the trick.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:45.10,1:27:46.64,Default,,0,0,0,,To the Taffy-Pulling Room.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:46.73,1:27:50.48,Default,,0,0,0,,The boy is in his mother's purse.\NBut be extremely careful.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:50.56,1:27:51.98,Default,,0,0,0,,[Mrs. Teevee stuttering]
Dialogue: 0,1:27:52.48,1:27:54.40,Default,,0,0,0,,What's he saying?
Dialogue: 0,1:27:54.65,1:27:57.24,Default,,0,0,0,,No, I won't hold you responsible.
Dialogue: 0,1:27:58.49,1:28:02.20,Default,,0,0,0,,And now, my dearest lady,\Nit's time to say goodbye.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:02.41,1:28:04.20,Default,,0,0,0,,No, don't speak.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:04.41,1:28:08.66,Default,,0,0,0,,For some moments in life,\Nthere are no words. Run along now.
Dialogue: 0,1:28:08.83,1:28:11.54,Default,,0,0,0,,[Mrs. Teevee mumbles incoherently]
Dialogue: 0,1:28:15.17,1:28:17.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Adieu.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:28:17.67,1:28:20.34,Default,,0,0,0,," Parting is such sweet sorrow. "
Dialogue: 0,1:28:26.22,1:28:28.26,Default,,0,0,0,,[Slow instrumental music]
Dialogue: 0,1:28:29.35,1:28:32.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}[Singing] Oompa Loompa Doompadee Do{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:28:32.94,1:28:35.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}I've got another puzzle for you{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:28:36.48,1:28:39.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oompa Loompa Doompada Dee{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:28:39.95,1:28:42.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If you are wise you'll listen to me{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:28:43.49,1:28:46.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}What do you get from a glut of TV?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:28:46.70,1:28:49.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}A pain in the neck and an IQ of three{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:28:50.46,1:28:53.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Why don't you try simply reading a book?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:28:53.96,1:28:56.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Or could you just not bear to look?{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:28:56.59,1:28:58.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You'll get no{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:29:01.17,1:29:04.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You'll get no commercials{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:29:04.18,1:29:08.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oompa Loompa Doompadee Da{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:29:08.68,1:29:12.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If you like reading, you will go far{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:29:12.56,1:29:15.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You will live in happiness, too{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:29:16.31,1:29:17.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Like the{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:29:18.19,1:29:19.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oompa{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:29:20.19,1:29:23.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Oompa Loompa Doompadee Do{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:29:26.91,1:29:30.83,Default,,0,0,0,,So much to do: Invoices, bills, letters.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:31.83,1:29:34.33,Default,,0,0,0,,I must answer that note from the Queen.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:35.17,1:29:38.84,Default,,0,0,0,,What's gonna happen to the other kids?\NAugustus and Veruca?
Dialogue: 0,1:29:38.92,1:29:42.17,Default,,0,0,0,,My dear boy, I promise you\Nthey'll be quite all right.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:42.26,1:29:47.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}When they leave here, they'll be restored\Nto their normal, terrible old selves.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:29:47.93,1:29:50.68,Default,,0,0,0,,But maybe they'll be\Na little bit wiser for the wear.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:50.77,1:29:52.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't worry about it.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:52.43,1:29:54.85,Default,,0,0,0,,What do we do now, Mr. Wonka?
Dialogue: 0,1:29:55.27,1:29:59.15,Default,,0,0,0,,I hope you enjoyed yourselves.\NExcuse me for not showing you out.
Dialogue: 0,1:29:59.23,1:30:02.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Straight up the stairs, you'll find it.\NI'm busy. A whole day wasted.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:02.74,1:30:04.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Goodbye to you both.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:05.95,1:30:07.37,Default,,0,0,0,,[Door closing]
Dialogue: 0,1:30:08.28,1:30:11.45,Default,,0,0,0,,What happened?\NDid we do something wrong?
Dialogue: 0,1:30:12.04,1:30:13.96,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't know, Charlie.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:14.54,1:30:16.63,Default,,0,0,0,,But I'm going to find out.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:22.05,1:30:23.84,Default,,0,0,0,,[Clock ticking]
Dialogue: 0,1:30:34.27,1:30:37.40,Default,,0,0,0,,GRANDPA: Mr. Wonka?\NWONKA: I am extraordinarily busy, sir.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:37.48,1:30:40.32,Default,,0,0,0,,I just wanted to ask about the chocolate.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:40.40,1:30:43.82,Default,,0,0,0,,The lifetime supply of chocolate.\NFor Charlie.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:44.32,1:30:45.86,Default,,0,0,0,,When does he get it?
Dialogue: 0,1:30:45.99,1:30:48.12,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: He doesn't.\NGRANDPA: Why not?
Dialogue: 0,1:30:48.32,1:30:50.45,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: Because he broke the rules.
Dialogue: 0,1:30:50.66,1:30:53.37,Default,,0,0,0,,What rules?\NWe didn't see any rules, did we?
Dialogue: 0,1:30:53.45,1:30:55.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Wrong, sir!
Dialogue: 0,1:30:55.91,1:30:59.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Under Section 37-B\Nof the contract signed by him...
Dialogue: 0,1:30:59.58,1:31:03.58,Default,,0,0,0,,it states quite clearly that\Nall offers shall become null and void if...
Dialogue: 0,1:31:03.67,1:31:07.01,Default,,0,0,0,,And you can read it for yourself\Nin this photostat copy:
Dialogue: 0,1:31:07.09,1:31:08.68,Default,,0,0,0,," I, the undersigned...
Dialogue: 0,1:31:08.76,1:31:11.76,Default,,0,0,0,," shall forfeit all rights,\Nprivileges, and licenses...
Dialogue: 0,1:31:11.85,1:31:14.06,Default,,0,0,0,," herein contained," etc.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:14.27,1:31:17.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}'"Fax mentis incendium\Ngloriae culpum, '"etc.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:31:21.36,1:31:24.66,Default,,0,0,0,,It's all there, black and white,\Nclear as crystal!
Dialogue: 0,1:31:24.86,1:31:27.07,Default,,0,0,0,,You stole Fizzy-Lifting drinks!
Dialogue: 0,1:31:27.28,1:31:31.03,Default,,0,0,0,,You bumped into the ceiling which\Nnow has to be washed and sterilized!
Dialogue: 0,1:31:31.12,1:31:33.16,Default,,0,0,0,,So you get nothing!
Dialogue: 0,1:31:33.37,1:31:34.66,Default,,0,0,0,,You lose!
Dialogue: 0,1:31:34.87,1:31:36.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Good day, sir!
Dialogue: 0,1:31:37.79,1:31:39.38,Default,,0,0,0,,You're a crook.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:39.46,1:31:42.46,Default,,0,0,0,,You're a cheat and a swindler,\Nthat's what you are.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:42.54,1:31:44.63,Default,,0,0,0,,How can you do a thing like this?
Dialogue: 0,1:31:44.71,1:31:48.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Build up a little boy's hopes and\Nthen smash all his dreams to pieces.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:48.55,1:31:50.59,Default,,0,0,0,,You're an inhuman monster!
Dialogue: 0,1:31:50.68,1:31:52.35,Default,,0,0,0,,I said, good day!
Dialogue: 0,1:31:56.56,1:31:59.44,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, Charlie. Let's get out of here.
Dialogue: 0,1:31:59.52,1:32:02.48,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll get even with him\Nif it's the last thing I ever do.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:02.56,1:32:05.48,Default,,0,0,0,,If Slugworth wants a Gobstopper,\Nhe'll get one.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:28.47,1:32:29.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Mr. Wonka.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:38.35,1:32:42.81,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: " So shines a good deed\Nin a weary world. "
Dialogue: 0,1:32:44.56,1:32:45.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Charlie.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:47.40,1:32:49.03,Default,,0,0,0,,My boy.
Dialogue: 0,1:32:49.69,1:32:50.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}You've won!{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:32:51.20,1:32:53.20,Default,,0,0,0,,You did it!
Dialogue: 0,1:32:53.28,1:32:55.99,Default,,0,0,0,,I just knew you would!
Dialogue: 0,1:32:57.58,1:33:00.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Forgive me for putting you through this.\NPlease forgive me.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:33:00.66,1:33:03.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Come in, Mr. Wilkinson.\NCharlie, meet Mr. Wilkinson.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:03.88,1:33:05.47,Default,,0,0,0,,WILKINSON: Pleasure.\NCHARLIE: Slugworth.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:05.54,1:33:08.21,Default,,0,0,0,,No, that's not Slugworth.\NHe works for me.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:08.30,1:33:10.72,Default,,0,0,0,,CHARLIE: For you?\NWONKA: I had to test you, Charlie.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:10.80,1:33:13.76,Default,,0,0,0,,And you passed the test. You won!
Dialogue: 0,1:33:13.84,1:33:16.34,Default,,0,0,0,,GRANDPA: Won what?\NWONKA: The jackpot, my dear sir.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:16.43,1:33:19.14,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: The grand and glorious jackpot.\NCHARLIE: The chocolate?
Dialogue: 0,1:33:19.22,1:33:22.60,Default,,0,0,0,,The chocolate, yes.\NBut that's just the beginning.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:22.69,1:33:26.40,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}We have to get on.\NWe have so much time and so little to do.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:33:26.48,1:33:28.36,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: Strike that. Reverse it.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:28.57,1:33:30.20,Default,,0,0,0,,This way, please.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:30.74,1:33:32.83,Default,,0,0,0,,We'll take the Wonkavator.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:33.36,1:33:35.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Step in, Charlie. Grandpa Joe, sir.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:43.92,1:33:48.01,Default,,0,0,0,,- This is the great glass Wonkavator.\N- It's an elevator.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:48.09,1:33:50.59,Default,,0,0,0,,It's a Wonkavator.\NAn elevator only goes up and down.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:50.67,1:33:54.22,Default,,0,0,0,,But the Wonkavator goes sideways,\Nslantways, longways, back ways...
Dialogue: 0,1:33:54.30,1:33:57.68,Default,,0,0,0,,CHARLIE: And front ways?\NWONKA:... and any other ways you think of.
Dialogue: 0,1:33:58.01,1:34:02.31,Default,,0,0,0,,It can take you to any room by pressing\None of these buttons. Any button.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:02.52,1:34:05.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Press a button and zing, you're off.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:05.94,1:34:08.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}And up until now, I've pressed them all.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:34:08.86,1:34:10.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Except one.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:11.11,1:34:12.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}This one.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:34:13.36,1:34:15.53,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: Go ahead, Charlie.\NCHARLIE: Me?
Dialogue: 0,1:34:18.87,1:34:20.12,Default,,0,0,0,,There it goes.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:22.29,1:34:23.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Hold on tight.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:34:24.12,1:34:26.96,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm not exactly sure\Nwhat's going to happen.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:27.71,1:34:31.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Faster. If we don't pick up speed,\Nwe won't get through.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:31.21,1:34:32.92,Default,,0,0,0,,CHARLIE: Get through what?
Dialogue: 0,1:34:33.42,1:34:35.63,Default,,0,0,0,,- You mean, we're going...\N- Up and out.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:35.72,1:34:38.85,Default,,0,0,0,,But the roof is glass.\NIt'll shatter into a thousand pieces.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:38.93,1:34:41.35,Default,,0,0,0,,- We'll be cut to ribbons.\N- Probably.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:45.06,1:34:46.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Hold on, everybody.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:34:47.90,1:34:50.24,Default,,0,0,0,,Here it comes.
Dialogue: 0,1:34:54.28,1:34:56.49,Default,,0,0,0,,[Light instrumental music]
Dialogue: 0,1:35:05.12,1:35:08.92,Default,,0,0,0,,GRANDPA: You did it. Congratulations.\NWONKA: Get up, take a look.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:09.00,1:35:11.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Grandpa, our town looks so pretty\Nfrom up here.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:11.75,1:35:14.92,Default,,0,0,0,,GRANDPA: Look over here, Charlie.\NI think I see our house.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:16.76,1:35:18.76,Default,,0,0,0,,GRANDPA: It really looks beautiful.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:18.84,1:35:20.80,Default,,0,0,0,,There's my school, Grandpa.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:21.18,1:35:23.98,Default,,0,0,0,,[Light instrumental music continues]
Dialogue: 0,1:35:26.73,1:35:29.28,Default,,0,0,0,,How did you like the chocolate factory?
Dialogue: 0,1:35:29.35,1:35:32.27,Default,,0,0,0,,I think it's the most wonderful place\Nin the whole world.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:32.36,1:35:34.53,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: I'm very pleased\Nto hear you say that...
Dialogue: 0,1:35:34.61,1:35:36.90,Default,,0,0,0,,because I'm giving it to you.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:38.03,1:35:40.45,Default,,0,0,0,,CHARLIE: What?\NWONKA: That's all right, isn't it?
Dialogue: 0,1:35:40.53,1:35:43.37,Default,,0,0,0,,GRANDPA: You're giving Charlie-\NWONKA: I can't go on forever.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:43.45,1:35:45.70,Default,,0,0,0,,WONKA: And I don't really want to try.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:45.79,1:35:48.84,Default,,0,0,0,,So who can I trust\Nto run the factory when I leave...
Dialogue: 0,1:35:48.92,1:35:50.88,Default,,0,0,0,,and take care\Nof the Oompa Loompas for me?
Dialogue: 0,1:35:50.96,1:35:52.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Not a grownup.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:52.46,1:35:55.88,Default,,0,0,0,,A grownup would want to do everything\Nhis own way, not mine.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:55.96,1:35:59.71,Default,,0,0,0,,That's why I decided a long time ago\Nthat I had to find a child.
Dialogue: 0,1:35:59.80,1:36:03.22,Default,,0,0,0,,A very honest, loving child...
Dialogue: 0,1:36:03.72,1:36:07.22,Default,,0,0,0,,to whom I can tell all my most precious\Ncandy-making secrets.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:07.31,1:36:09.98,Default,,0,0,0,,CHARLIE: So, you sent the Golden Tickets?\NWONKA: Right.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:10.06,1:36:12.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\i1}The factory's yours.\NYou can move in immediately.{\i0}
Dialogue: 0,1:36:12.81,1:36:14.81,Default,,0,0,0,,GRANDPA: And me?\NWONKA: Absolutely.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:14.98,1:36:17.57,Default,,0,0,0,,CHARLIE: What happens to the-\NWONKA: The whole family.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:17.65,1:36:19.61,Default,,0,0,0,,I want you to bring them all.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:23.16,1:36:24.91,Default,,0,0,0,,But, Charlie...
Dialogue: 0,1:36:25.41,1:36:29.37,Default,,0,0,0,,don't forget what happened to the man\Nwho suddenly got everything he wanted.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:29.46,1:36:30.84,Default,,0,0,0,,CHARLIE: What happened?
Dialogue: 0,1:36:30.92,1:36:33.26,Default,,0,0,0,,He lived happily ever after.
Dialogue: 0,1:36:35.17,1:36:37.84,Default,,0,0,0,,[Sweeping instrumental music]
Dialogue: 0,1:37:30.27,1:37:31.31,Default,,0,0,0,,English - SDH
